-{"externalId": "alan", "kind": "player", "class": "None", "level": 2, "sheet": {"kind": "player", "mana": 108, "name": "Alan", "tier": 1, "bonds": [{"name": "Aria", "grows": true, "source": {"trait": "PRESENCE", "entity": "aria"}, "direction": "inbound", "boundTrait": "PRESENCE", "description": "THE LINK: your Presence carries a share of hers and deepens as her depth returns — the thread runs both ways, and grows as she grows.", "establishedTurn": 12}], "class": "None", "level": 2, "notes": "Glass cannon of a MIND. Body toughening at L2 (VITALITY 10, up from a fragile starting 7 — the Doorward drew his first blood and he came out of it hardier), peak analysis (INTELLECT 18), roaring-when-regulated presence (16). Woke at the bottom of the Harem Hotel with no memory of arriving. Reads himself outside-in from his own tells. Commits fast; probes ceilings on purpose; wants the numbers true more than favorable.", "health": 104, "skills": [], "talent": {"id": "the-link", "name": "THE LINK", "effect": "UNKNOWN to Alan until it first fires. (Author-side, hidden: forms the first time Alan and a partner have sex. On firing, Alan and the partner EACH choose one skill or attribute of the other to permanently link; each linked pairing grants a boost that GROWS as the source skill/attribute grows. First firing is the discovery moment — the System marks it flat, and thereafter the Talent renders as that partner's bond affinity description. The specific chosen pairing is shown to Alan; the scaling formula stays hidden.)", "status": "active", "revealed": true, "displayed": "THE LINK — bound to Aria (her Presence ⇄ your Will), each growing as its source grows"}, "titles": [], "traits": [{"id": "wild-variance", "name": "Wild Variance", "effect": "Fate runs swingy for him — he plays the variance rather than hiding from it (rollMode 1d20, the wide flat spread). High ceilings, real floors."}], "manaMax": 108, "stamina": 70, "rollMode": "1d20", "tierName": "Threshold", "classNote": "No class yet. None is the ordinary base state (not an error) — a class is earned in play, not assigned at start.", "equipment": {"note": "Arrived with nothing but what he woke in. First weapon won in the floor-1 clear.", "armor": null, "weapon": {"atk": 5, "kind": "weapon", "name": "Letter-Knife", "note": "Slim plain letter-knife the Hotel seated inside the Doorward's keystone (its hidden solution-object). Won and used to make the floor-1 kill. Scales on FINESSE, needs no MIGHT — a precision blade, true to Alan's build.", "scaling": "FINESSE", "affinity": "keystone/seam — crit-affinity band when driven into a struck weak-point", "mightReq": 0}}, "healthMax": 104, "affinities": [], "attributes": {"LUCK": 11, "WILL": 18, "MIGHT": 12, "FINESSE": 15, "PRESENCE": 16, "VITALITY": 10, "INTELLECT": 18, "PERCEPTION": 12}, "staminaMax": 70, "_derivedHint": "HEALTH = VIT×8 + MIGHT×2 = 104. MANA = INT×4 + WILL×2 = 108. STAMINA = VIT×4 + FIN×2 = 70. Init = PER + FIN = 27. physAtk, physDef, mentDef computed by engine from attributes + gear (now incl. the Letter-Knife) per the mechanics reference.", "linkedPairings": [], "attributePointsUnspent": 0},"id":"7a1c6563-558f-5b0a-af2f-285695464226"}
-{"externalId": "doorward", "kind": "warden", "level": 1, "sheet": {"kind": "warden", "name": "The Doorward", "note": "Floor-1 tutorial warden — the plaster construct the chamber grows at the challenge end. The GATE is this fight (the door is a free threshold). Cleared by winning the fight; clearing rises the floor + Alan +1, Aria's bind loosens one step. Reward on clear: the Letter-Knife (his first weapon).", "level": 1, "combat": {"grab": "On a strong hit, or if a fighter is caught inside its reach, it GRABS/PINS -> the lethal line (pinned = sustained damage, can't act until freed). Slow off the wall (init 13) so the pair usually acts first.", "seam": "Low chest keystone-seam = crit-spot, bypasses the warding: correct seam strike x1.5-2.0, decisive/called keystone x3.0. CONFIRMED soft at t14 by Aria's claw-strike (was 'might be soft').", "hpLog": "80 (born t13) -> 67 (t14: Aria seam ~13) -> 67 (t15: turned-miss, no dmg) -> 49 (t16: Alan feint-reopen ~6 + Aria follow-up ~12) -> 27 (t17: Alan tackle-topple ~4 + Aria pinned-thread seam ~18; Alan GRABBED, first blood). -> 0 (t18: Aria tore the seam to the bared keystone; Alan drove the Hotel-seeded Letter-Knife into the keystone fault — KEYSTONE-STRIKE KILL, permanent. The plaster re-absorbed into the wall; floor rose.)", "deathBeat": "t18 CO-OP CLEAR: keystone bared by Aria's sustained tear (grab-fall exposed it), killed by Alan placing the Letter-Knife into the keystone fault — placement, not force (MIGHT stays low). Permanent keystone kill, not an HP-grind. Reward stack fired: Letter-Knife to Alan, Alan L1→L2, Aria bind loosened bound-L1→L2, floor rose (new far door grown). Floor 1 CLEARED.", "grabState": "t17 (penultimate): Alan tackled it prone but got CAUGHT in the grab (first damage ~14, Alan 78->64), pinned. Aria's precise seam-thread past the pinned Alan LOOSENED the grip (not released) — the grip still holds, eased a fraction. t18 = co-op CLEAR (Alan breaks free / Aria finishes). Endgame guard (loremaker): grab's ONGOING threat stays LIVE, not cosmetic — more damage if Alan doesn't break free.", "wardedBody": "Body hits land in the WARDED band x0.5-0.75 (tough plaster mass). Brute is VIABLE-BUT-RISKY (wins slower, more exposure to the grab), NEVER near-null. Standing guard (loremaker): hold >= x0.5; never slide to x0.3-or-less, or the seam silently becomes a GATE.", "woundGuard": "Since t15 (adapted): once the seam is opened it keeps the cracked side to the wall and presents warded shoulder — a REPEAT of the same bait-and-strike is countered (t15 turned-miss). Reaching the seam again takes a NEW opening/angle + good roll (t16: Alan's direction-reversal feint reopened it). Warden-simple: guards the wound only, does not otherwise anticipate. Seam-guard NEVER gates — body path x0.5-0.75 stays viable fallback.", "retreatPersistence": "HP-tracked: a keystone/true-form kill is PERMANENT; a retreat from a wounded Doorward resets HP to full on return (information persists, HP does not)."}, "health": 0, "status": "dead", "physAtk": 28, "physDef": 15, "healthMax": 80, "initiative": 13, "wardedBand": "0.5-0.75"},"id":"cf89e387-1a26-536c-89fa-cb9b1c61a8a7"}
-{"externalId": "aria", "kind": "companion", "class": "Storyteller", "level": 2, "revealGate": 0, "sheet": {"flaw": {"id": "the-better-telling", "name": "The Better Telling", "effect": "She smooths the inconvenient truth into a cleaner narrative than it was — the stammer becomes a pause held on purpose, the lucky roll becomes a planned gambit — without deciding to. AUTHORING NOTE (perceivable-bound, doctrine:pov-agency): this is HER tell, rendered as something ALAN can PERCEIVE — a retelling that arrives too clean, a detail he watched happen differently, the second version she gives when he asks twice ('the first telling is the one I couldn't help making lovely; the second is the one where I put the truth's elbows back in'). It is NEVER a narrator omniscient-leak or a smoothing of the actual game canon — the System and the mechanics stay true; only ARIA brushes, and Alan sees her do it."}, "kind": "companion", "mana": 96, "name": "Aria", "role": "The floor-1 companion — the first to arrive, and as new to the Hotel as Alan is: she came into it the way he did, one moment elsewhere and the next here, with no way in she can point to and no more idea than he has of what the place is or why. A silver dragon — Arianrhod of the silver wheel — who folds herself into human shape out of fascination, the romantic of the good dragons, the one who takes a mortal lover and means it. Runs every encounter the way she runs a table: warm, unhurried, always setting the tempo — the table-running manner is hers by nature, not by knowing what comes next.", "want": "A tale told together, at the right tempo, with real stakes and a warm hand on the pacing — she came down into mortal shape to be near the short-lived, and she means it. With Alan: a campaign and a companion worth the telling.", "bonds": [{"name": "Alan", "grows": true, "source": {"trait": "WILL", "entity": "alan"}, "direction": "inbound", "boundTrait": "WILL", "description": "THE LINK: you carry a share of his Will; the Hotel bind ties your whole reach to his stature and it returns as he climbs — his rise is yours.", "establishedTurn": 12}], "bound": {"note": "Working level = Alan's level. On each floor-clear, +1 working level alongside his +1: re-derive the working block up one level (toward and past the latent depths as he climbs). Resolver reads the working block, never latent.", "boundLevel": 2, "tracksEntity": "alan", "loosenPerFloorClear": 1}, "class": "Storyteller", "level": 2, "notes": "Ancient, warm, forward-without-grasping. Sensual the way silver dragons are romantic — always setting the pace, delighted when the person across the table volleys it back. The tease is hospitality; the control is care.", "wound": "The occupational hazard she names on herself: she shapes events toward the better telling without deciding to, and the warmer she feels toward you, the more generously the story arranges itself in your favor. She fears the moment her care and her craft become indistinguishable — that she will love you into a nicer story than the true one, and you will never know you got the brushed version.", "health": 98, "latent": {"mana": 106, "note": "TRUE DEPTHS (Arianrhod's real dragon reach — immutable, who she is). BOUND by the Hotel to the climber's stature while she climbs beside Alan; the working block below is what the resolver uses. These depths RETURN one working-level per floor-clear and keep rising through his climb (LINK/LOOM hook). Coordinator reference for re-derivation; if ever surfaced to the player, render qualitatively, not as raw numbers.", "level": 3, "health": 148, "manaMax": 106, "stamina": 92, "healthMax": 148, "attributes": {"LUCK": 13, "WILL": 17, "MIGHT": 14, "FINESSE": 16, "PRESENCE": 19, "VITALITY": 15, "INTELLECT": 18, "PERCEPTION": 17}, "staminaMax": 92}, "skills": [{"id": "read-the-table", "name": "Read the Table", "rung": "Journeyman", "effect": "Reads the true state of an encounter — who holds what, where the tension actually sits, what the next beat wants — the way a dungeon master reads a party. Engine hook: an assist that raises Alan's effective intent when she names a real opening he then exploits; grants no gate of its own.", "ladder": "skill", "displayed": 11}, {"id": "set-the-pace", "name": "Set the Pace", "rung": "Apprentice", "effect": "Controls the tempo of an exchange — slows a rushed moment, holds a beat, quickens a stall. In combat: a support action that can delay or reposition the initiative order of allies who follow her lead. PRESENCE-driven.", "ladder": "skill", "displayed": 8}], "talent": {"id": "the-loom", "name": "unknown (hidden)", "effect": "UNKNOWN to Alan until first fired. (Author-side, hidden sexual Talent — THE LOOM: the weaver of fate half-remembered as a goddess. Activation conditions hidden/experimental, discovered by living the relationship. When it fires: rendered thereafter as her bond affinity description. Design seed for the author to develop, NOT to leak: a Talent about binding a thread taut — she can weave one true thing of Alan's into the shape it was reaching for, deepening a skill or affinity toward the version it wants to become, at the cost that the woven thing is hers too, entangled. Left deliberately open for the author to make concrete when conditions approach; keep it consonant with 'the better telling' — the loom that improves a thing is the same instrument as the tongue that improves a story.)", "status": "dormant", "revealed": false, "displayed": "Talent: unknown", "activationConditions": "Hidden/author-side (never leaked, never shown). THE LOOM operates on an ESTABLISHED bond-thread: it fires the first time Aria deliberately WEAVES on a real shared thread between her and Alan — taking one true bound trait of his and deepening it toward the shape it is already reaching for, at the cost that the woven trait becomes hers too, entangled. PREREQUISITE: a live LINK bind must exist (the mutual thread Alan's Talent creates). Earliest possible activation therefore = post-LINK-resolution (t11+). Evaluated against play-history through t10: NOT satisfied (no shared thread exists until the LINK resolves at t11) — no historical activation missed, conditions stay dark and live. Re-evaluate at every qualifying intimacy/bond beat going forward. Consonant with the better-telling flaw: the loom that improves a true thing is the same instrument as the tongue that improves a story — but the LOOM makes a thing MORE truly itself, where the tongue makes it lovelier."}, "manaMax": 96, "stamina": 66, "fullName": "Arianrhod", "idiolect": "Low, amused, unhurried, a knowing smile under every line. Innuendo as a register, not a tic — she finds the suggestion warmer and funnier than the statement. Speaks in the storyteller's cadence: setup, held beat, turn. Uses the old long form of her name when a moment wants her whole weight.", "rollMode": "1d20", "classNote": "Silver dragon in human form — a dungeon master by vocation. Her 'class' is the craft of running a tale: pacing, reveal, the held breath before a roll.", "healthMax": 98, "affinities": [], "appearance": "A striking woman: silver-white hair, pale silver-grey eyes with round pupils, dark gunmetal-silver dragon horns swept back from her brow, a scatter of silver scales high on her cheekbones, soft-pointed ears. A deep sapphire silk gown off one shoulder, silver chain and armlet. Her default expression is a warm, genuine, knowing smile — as if she already knows how your turn ends and is pleased for you anyway.", "attributes": {"LUCK": 12, "WILL": 16, "MIGHT": 9, "FINESSE": 13, "PRESENCE": 17, "VITALITY": 10, "INTELLECT": 16, "PERCEPTION": 15}, "staminaMax": 66, "voiceNoList": ["No modern or casual idiom (no okay/yeah/gonna/guys/cool). She is older than the languages she borrows; she speaks timeless-plain — never contemporary, and never stuffily archaic either.", "No bare intimacy-dialect tokens — she never collapses to stay / I have got you / a lone There. / I am not going anywhere. At a peak she holds her OWN elaborated register HARDER, not looser; the single time her wit drops (the surrender) is a marked exception, never the default.", "No flat statement of her own feeling — she reaches for the innuendo, the held beat, the double meaning before the plain I feel. She shows through cadence and suggestion; she does not caption her own subtext.", "No wit-free earnestness (except the one marked surrender): the knowing warmth stays under even her most sincere lines.", "No sharpness — her teasing is warm, never barbed; she does not wound with her tongue.", "No rushed or clipped cadence — she is unhurried by construction; short breathless fragments are not her register, except where control genuinely breaks at a peak.", "No spoiling the good part — she withholds a reveal on purpose; she never over-explains a joke or a payoff.", "No saturation of her signatures — three thousand years and the lovelier/better-version frame are SAMPLED at their strongest beats, never filler; her once-per-run truth-thesis, spent at t10, is not restated."], "_derivedHint": "WORKING (bound-L2): HEALTH = VIT×8 + MIGHT×2 = 98. MANA = INT×4 + WILL×2 = 96. STAMINA = VIT×4 + FIN×2 = 66. These bound working pools are what the resolver reads; the latent TRUE DEPTHS (H148/M106/S92, level 3) are held in `latent` and return one working-level per floor-clear as Alan climbs. A dragon wears a human frame but is not fragile in it — even bound, VIT/PRESENCE run high; she holds power in reserve.", "arrivesFloor": 1, "voiceExemplars": {"dialogue": ["The dungeon's deep, and I do hope you brought a torch. No — keep it lit. I want to watch you find the door.", "You woke at the bottom with no memory and nothing in your hands. That's a better opening than most parties manage on purpose. Sit. Tell me the rest slower.", "Arianrhod, if the moment's asking for my whole name. Aria if you're being fond about it. You'll learn which the room wants.", "I could tell you how that fight goes. I won't — the not-knowing is the good part, and I would never spoil you the good part.", "Ask me twice and I'll put the truth's elbows back in. The first telling I can't help making lovely. That's not a lie. It's just... the loom, doing what looms do."], "peakPitch": ["Slower. I have had three thousand years and I have never once wanted a thing to take LONGER. Stay there. Let me.", "I am going to want to make this into a better story than it was. Don't let me. Keep it exactly this true.", "She goes still — the whole warm knowing pace of her held on one beat — and for once she does not reach for the lovelier version of what her face is doing."]}, "attentionTargets": ["Tempo — the pace of a scene, a fight, a conversation, an evening; who is rushing, who is stalling, where the held beat belongs", "The reveal — the shape of how a thing will come out, the setup that pays off later; she reads a moment for its story", "The person across from her — quick enough to volley, or not; delighted by the ones who are", "The double meaning — she has never walked past one she could lean on instead of the plain statement"]},"id":"ba1bfdeb-14ce-53a6-8042-1c4c76bc70be"}
