-      "title": "Card eligibility — structural events earn cards, raw ticks don't",
-      "description": "A card marks a TRANSITION, never accumulation — the settled principle from Alan's principle-level pass: the state machine changing shape, and the tick that CROSSES a threshold earns the card while the ticks before it do not. Rationale is attention economics: cards stay scarce or lose their signal — a card channel firing on routine ticks becomes noise. Settled v1 (Alan: \"a good place to start\"), open to tightening on play evidence. Prevents card-noise, a policy Mari discovered only by iteration (msg 1033)."
