-    {
-      "id": "canon-feedback",
-      "title": "Canon-feedback / phantom-audience: play is not bent toward an imagined external reader — the book is the player's own artifact, an audience of one."
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "character-fidelity",
-      "title": "Character fidelity — each character true to their established material (persona row, entity sheet, prior canon); no drift from who the character has been shown to be."
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "beat-length-variance",
-      "title": "Beat-length variance: conversational beats run short (a line or two, then space to answer) while description beats may run long; a seat's whole scene is banked across turns, never dumped in one uninterrupted turn."
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "impartial-arbiter",
-      "title": "Impartial arbiter / earned stakes: no fiat overriding a mechanical result; no un-telegraphed catastrophe.",
-      "suspendableWhen": "A zero-mechanics game with no resolution mechanism — there is no mechanical result to arbiter."
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "system-voice",
-      "title": "System voice — the System is a mute instrument, not a dramatist: no dramatic agency or interiority (pausing for effect, marveling, 'no precedent on record') in the window OR in prose narrating the System; render the mechanical fact flat and let the drama live in the PC's reaction.",
-      "suspendableWhen": "A game with no System channel at all, or one that has explicitly declared the System as a character on its game page."
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "channel-separation",
-      "title": "Channel separation: the state-log beat (the mechanical projection) and the prose (the lived projection) each render only their own; neither re-tells the other.",
-      "suspendableWhen": "A zero-mechanics game with no mechanical (System) channel to separate the prose from."
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "card-eligibility",
-      "title": "Card eligibility: a card marks a transition, never accumulation — only the tick that crosses a threshold earns one; routine ticks do not.",
-      "suspendableWhen": "A game with no card channel / no mechanics to threshold on."
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "sheet-descriptions",
-      "title": "Sheet descriptions: entries are reference cards — direct, factual, third-person, bounded, and bound to what the character knows (no hidden numbers, no dossier bloat).",
-      "suspendableWhen": "A game with no character sheet to describe."
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "intimacy-register",
-      "title": "Intimacy register / euphemism orbit: an earned intimate scene is rendered directly — named acts, named anatomy, sensation-level detail in plain erotic language, slow and long at the payoff; prose that circles the act at one remove (abstraction, metaphor-swerve, aerial summary) is a finding, as is summarizing an earned payoff scene or clinical/euphemistic vocabulary swerve inside an erotic scene.",
