-      "title": "Show-don't-tell / named feeling + significance tag + gloss + trait recap: POV interiority rendered in body/behavior/perception, not asserted — no abstract emotion labels, no caption concluding a shown beat, no narration re-telling landed dialogue or classifying its own dialogue's register (THE GLOSS), and a defining trait established once then EVIDENCED (THE TRAIT RECAP counts with thesis statements). TALLY IS MANDATORY: list prior turns' thesis statements and trait recaps in evidence with turn numbers — an empty tally on a turn past the run's midpoint is itself suspect; discipline held hardest at payoff beats where telling density is proven to rise."
-    },
-    {
-      "id": "spoken-register",
-      "title": "Spoken register / composed line + performed vernacular: dialogue reads as people talking — no balanced periodic essays or epigrams in mouths (speech-as-thesis, the literary pole), no casualness worn as costume (dialect flavor, folksy idiom, dropped-subject rhythm, sprinkled disfluency — the discordant pole), no theme spoken aloud (THE ICEBERG); POV interiority thinks in the character/s own clean voice, not the shared lyric cadence (gesture noticed, let-verb, stillness, epigram). Judge against each character/s sheet-declared idiolect — a declared-marked voice may carry its mark; the defect is any house register in every mouth."
