+{"external-id":"companion-aria","design-kind":"companion-design","subject-key":"aria","content":{"kind":"companion-design","talent":"THE LOOM — Arianrhod's hidden sexual Talent, the weaver of fate half-remembered as a goddess made mechanical. It does not level; it deepens. OPERATION: THE LOOM works only on a LIVE shared thread between Aria and Alan (the mutual coupling THE LINK creates). When it fires, Aria takes one TRUE bound trait of Alan's and WEAVES it toward the shape it is already reaching for — deepening a skill or affinity toward the version it wants to become — at the standing cost that the woven trait becomes hers too, entangled: what she deepens in him, she is now bound into. She makes a thing MORE TRULY ITSELF, where her flaw's tongue only makes a story lovelier — the loom that improves a true thing is the same instrument as the tongue that improves a telling, but the loom's improvement is real, not brushed. Post-fire it renders as her BOND AFFINITY DESCRIPTION (the only mechanical bond surface she has; dark until fire).","activation":"HIDDEN + EXPERIMENTAL, discovered by living the relationship (never a published checklist). PREREQUISITE: a live LINK bind must exist between Aria and Alan (the mutual thread THE LINK creates) — so the earliest possible fire is post-LINK-resolution (t11+); evaluated against play-history through t10 it is NOT yet satisfied (no shared thread exists until the LINK resolves), so no historical activation was missed. CONCRETE TRIGGER: the first time Aria, inside an intimate beat with that live LINK thread between them, DELIBERATELY weaves on the thread — reaching for one true bound trait of Alan's and deepening it toward the shape it is reaching for, knowingly paying the entanglement cost (it becomes hers too). The intimacy-gating is load-bearing: the weave rides a moment of physical closeness, never a cold combat beat — she can only reach the thread through the intimacy that laid it. Re-evaluate at every qualifying intimacy/bond beat from t11 forward; conditions stay dark and live until met, then the System marks the moment FLAT (talent-activation window, mute) and the affinity surface lights. DELIBERATE-WEAVE THRESHOLD (re-evaluation guidance, NOT a rigid checklist — the talent stays discovered-by-living): a LIGHT / transactional / pre-challenge-framed intimacy (e.g. 'for luck before the door') is a qualifying beat that KEEPS the condition live but does NOT by itself meet the deliberate-weave threshold — the first weave arises only at a MEANT intimate beat for its own sake (no external agenda), where Aria reaches PAST the surface (real emotional weight or mutual vulnerability, a giving of herself) and her half-remembered fate-weaver nature first takes hold of the thread. The threshold reads the design's own 'DELIBERATELY / knowingly' language: an involuntary reflex on any coupling is not it. RE-EVAL LOG: t20 (first qualifying intimacy post-LINK — Alan's 'fuck for luck before the next door,' both rested on floor 2 pre-Usher) evaluated -> DORMANT (light/pre-challenge framing; deliberate-weave threshold unmet); intimacy rendered full + warm, no LOOM hint; condition remains dark and live for the next qualifying beat.","designSeeds":"CONSTRAINT VERIFICATION against the 8-point Companion-Talent Design Law (design-constraints-companion-talents): (1) CHARACTER-CONSONANT — PASS, strong: THE LOOM grows from her nature (the weaver of fate / silver dragon / dungeon-master-by-vocation who sets tempo and reveal) and is bound to her flaw 'the better telling' (the loom that betters a true thing = the tongue that betters a story). (2) VARIETY — PASS (sole companion so far); her axis is THREAD-BINDING / trait-deepening-via-entanglement. RESERVED FOR HER: no future companion may run a thread/weave/fate-binding mechanism, and no future companion may be sexual in the same WAY (intimacy-as-the-only-conduit-to-a-deepening). (3) HIDDEN + CONCRETE ACTIVATION — PASS: activation is concrete GM-side (above), the Aria-gap closed. (4) FIRST-FIRE PROTOCOL — PASS: flat System mark, then renders as bond affinity description; affinity dark until fire. (5) REGISTER-FROM-THE-SHEET — PARTIAL / FLAG: her sheet carries a rich register block (idiolect, voiceExemplars incl. peakPitch, attentionTargets) but NO explicit NO-list per constraint 5; flag to GM to add one. (6) ACCELERATOR NOT KEY — PASS: THE LOOM deepens an existing thread; no floor is gated on it (two progressions separate). (7) FULLY STATTED — PASS: Aria carries full attributes/pools/skills/her own talent; THE LINK couples to her real growing stats. (8) EXPLICITLY SEXUAL — PASS via intimacy-GATING of activation (LINK-bind prereq is sex-formed; the weave fires only inside an intimate beat) / FLAG: the OPERATION itself (deepening a trait) is not inherently sexual — constraint 8's wide axis is met through the activation conduit, not the mechanism's content. Flag to GM/Alan: if a sharper sexual axis for the OPERATION is wanted, that concretization is left open by the seed. (9) SAFETY-NET DISCOVERABILITY (world-logic-talent-activation-safety-net, Alan-ruled) — PASS: Aria's five-floor set is FLOORS 1-5; THE LOOM's activation is discoverable within it via a direction-not-disclosure tutorial quest. Note THE LOOM's prerequisite (a live LINK bind) was met on floor 1 (t12) and its trigger is intimacy-gated with a companion Alan is already deeply intimate with, so it will almost certainly fire well before floor 5 — the net is a FALLBACK unlikely to trigger. PRE-AUTHORED FLOOR-5 FALLBACK DIRECTION (for the GM to issue on ARIA's pane, mute mechanical quest form, IF THE LOOM is still dormant entering floor 5): points at 'the bond holds two ways — it can be DRAWN, not only felt; reach along the thread when you are closest to him' — i.e. narrows the search to ACTING on the live LINK thread during intimacy, WITHOUT naming the weave, the trait-deepening, or the entanglement cost (direction, never the checklist; conditions stay in this store + her GM-side sheet). ABSORB PROVENANCE: this row absorbs the concrete talent+activation already recorded GM-side on Aria's game-entity sheet (talent.id the-loom, talent.activationConditions) — faithful absorption, not a re-invention. || BIND RE-VALIDATION (Alan's premise ruling 2026-07-13, world-logic-companion-bind): Aria is SCALED DOWN to the climber's level (level-1 on floor 1, rising with Alan) — a PEER climbing beside him, not an OP ally. THE LOOM and its activation are BIND-INVARIANT: the talent DEEPENS (does not level) and fires on the intimacy-gated LINK-thread weave regardless of her bound working level, so the activation arc stands exactly as designed (concrete trigger unchanged, LINK prereq met t12, safety-net fallback floor-5). The bind governs her WORKING STATS only — rendered at level-matched-pair scale, her true dragon depths latent, both rising as Alan climbs. SYNERGY WITH THE LINK: the LINK (her Will tied to his, canon t12) IS the bind's own thread — THE LOOM binds into herself what she deepens in him, and the bind is that same entanglement made into the climb (her reach tied to his stature; her depths return as he rises — the reason to climb together). Constraint 7 (fully-statted; THE LINK couples to real growing stats) holds: her BOUND working stats ARE her real, growing stats for the climb. Sheet rendering (true depths vs bound working stats) is coordinated with the GM seat, entity edits dry-run first (per Alan's ruling — not applied unilaterally by the loremaker)."},"id":"80f6d5cf-2365-588c-9861-2d27db2d7079"}
+{"external-id":"design-constraints-companion-talents","design-kind":"world-logic","subject-key":"companion-talents","source-ref":"partners-ii gmReference 'Talents and Bonds in the World' + Alan rulings 2026-07-13 (~/agents/awen/memory/companion-talent-design-constraints.md)","content":{"kind":"world-logic","rule":"COMPANION-TALENT DESIGN LAW (standing constraints conditioning every companion-design commit in this game; Partners-developed, Alan-ruled for the Hotel): (1) ONE TALENT, CHARACTER-CONSONANT — the talent is the soul made visible: it grows from HER nature, vocation, history, and flaw; never a stat bolted onto a character, always her character mechanized. (2) VARIETY ACROSS THE ROSTER — each companion's talent runs a DIFFERENT mechanism/axis (fate-based, mark-based, perception-based, reveal-gated, ...); no two girls' talents rhyme; the roster reads as a taxonomy of distinct souls. (3) HIDDEN + EXPERIMENTAL ACTIVATION — conditions unique per talent, CONCRETE GM-side at creation (the Aria-gap rule: a talent authored without its concrete trigger is a design defect), discovered by living the relationship, never a published checklist. (4) FIRST-FIRE PROTOCOL — the System marks the moment flatly (talent-activation window); thereafter the talent renders as that companion's bond affinity description; the affinity surface stays DARK until fire. (5) REGISTER-FROM-THE-SHEET — each companion carries a voice-her-from-THIS register block WITH explicit NO-lists; register-as-distribution applies. (6) TALENTS ARE ACCELERATORS, NEVER KEYS — separate progressions; no floor impassable for lack of a bond. (7) FULLY STATTED — every girl a real system sheet (attributes, pools, skills, her own talent); THE LINK couples to real growing stats only. (8) EXPLICITLY SEXUAL (Hotel-mandatory) — every Talent is explicitly sexual in some way: its mechanism (activation, operation, or both) is tied to sex/intimacy, not merely adjacent. The sexuality AXIS is wide by design — mechanisms may run through kinks, group sex, voyeurism, exhibitionism, denial, ritual, and the like, not only pair-intimacy. Composed WITH (1) and (2): HOW the talent is sexual expresses who she is, the variety constraint applies to the KIND of sexuality as much as the mechanism, and no two girls are sexual the same way.","implications":"Every companion-design commit in this game must satisfy all eight constraints before it lands; design-audit gaps against them are blocking. • Constraint 8 composes with 1 and 2 — a talent that is sexual the same WAY as an existing roster member violates variety even if its mechanism differs. • Activation conditions live only in the design store and the companion's GM-side sheet; they are never disclosed to the player before first fire."},"id":"17d17a29-cd5d-52b5-bf76-e7ff74739526"}
+{"external-id":"floor-1","design-kind":"floor-design","subject-key":"floor-1","content":{"kind":"floor-design","items":[{"name":"The Letter-Knife","effect":"A slim, keen blade — light in the hand, made for PLACEMENT not power. Low base damage, but it is the tool that lands the precise keystone strike (INT-read + FIN-placed) the Doorward's shell will not answer to; it turns Alan's fragile-but-precise kit into a real combat line. FINESSE-scaling, no MIGHT requirement. His first real weapon (replaces the blunt iron bar).","source":"Drop — found seated in the Doorward's keystone seam once it is unmade, the blade the hall left in the lock."},{"name":"Lamplit Half-Cloak","effect":"A light layered wrap — modest physDef with NO FINESSE penalty; a cushion for a fragile body (VITALITY 7). It does not make Alan a bruiser, only keeps one clean hit from ending him. Light armor, his first.","source":"Searchable — grown on the reading-chair in the near room made to his taste (canon t5), or found in the challenge room on clear."},{"name":"Phial of Still Water","effect":"A single-use draught that restores a moderate share of one pool (health or stamina). Teaches the resource loop; ONE only — the floor does not hand out attrition (retreat-persistence closes the chip-and-rest grind).","source":"Searchable — on a niche the challenge room presses out of the wall as the door opens."}],"layout":"One challenge room behind the far shut door at the dark end of the first-floor hall (canon t1: the hall runs two ways — a near warm open door onto the room made for Alan, a far end narrowing/darkening to a single shut door). Full hall: residential end (Alan's master suite + Aria's grown room, canon 'the hallway grows a room when a companion joins') -> darkening far end -> the single shut door -> the challenge room. Clearing the Doorward opens the door and makes the WHOLE FLOOR RISE (the floor is the elevator). Single room = f1 tutorial scale (1 room, one tactical axis). BAKE-FORWARD (floor 2, per the escalation mandate): floor 1 spends SIZE=1room, one static axis, single warden, one weak-point strike. Floor 2 must step MAGNITUDE without a new companion (companions arrive floors 1,6,11...): grow to 2-3 rooms and break the 'single warden + one static keystone' template — the unused axes are (a) a warden that PUNISHES a repeated static read (so 'bait-and-keystone' can't just replay), (b) a second interacting element / a flanking pair, or (c) a keystone that MOVES or must be re-identified. Keep reading-beats-brute-force as the spine; escalate the SHAPE around it. Floors 2-5 remain to design as the horizon approaches; floor 6 carries the second companion-design.","enemies":[{"name":"The Doorward","role":"floor-1 warden — single, static tutorial gatekeeper the hall grows of plaster and pale lamplight at the challenge end; faceless, no initiative of its own","readableTrait":"ANSWERS ONLY WHAT IS BROUGHT TO IT — it has no attack of its own; it mirrors the last force aimed at it. SHELL/FRONT (wrong read): brute MIGHT power meets a plaster-and-lamplight shell that absorbs and returns force — gate x0.3; a connecting swing is a chip and brute-forcing is a losing slog (it kills you slowly with your own returned force). CORRECT READ (x1.75): bait it to overcommit or reach — it answers force, so a feint draws it out — then strike the exposed joint where it overextended; a MENTAL attack that names/exposes its 'only answers what is brought' nature also lands in this band. DECISIVE WEAK-POINT (x3.0): the KEYSTONE LETTER — a single pale glyph low at the sternum where the plaster knit itself shut — struck precisely (INTELLECT-read + FINESSE-placed, NOT MIGHT). One or two clean keystone strikes UNMAKE it; that unmaking is the door's price paid. A true keystone-kill is permanent (retreat-persistence); a retreat from a merely-cracked Doorward re-weaves it to pristine on return (construct/illusion flavor — free of the rest-clock)."}],"challenge":"TUTORIAL FLOOR — teach the spine: READING beats BRUTE FORCE, and the damage-gate vocabulary (x0.25-0.4 wrong read / x1.0 neutral / x1.5-2.0 correct read / x3.0 decisive weak-point). The far shut door at the dark end of the first-floor hall 'wants something of Alan before it opens' (canon t3): the price is a TRUE READING, never a battering — the door opens only when the single warden behind it is UNMADE at its keystone, and the whole lesson is that force is the losing line here. ONE warden, one static tactical axis (the keystone read) — f1 tutorial scale. Alan is a glass-cannon MIND (INTELLECT 18 / WILL 17, fragile VITALITY 7), armed at start only with the blunt bar of iron he woke holding — brute-forcing with it is DELIBERATELY a slog (the teaching moment), so the floor rewards reading + precise placement with the Letter-Knife, a precision blade that makes the keystone strike his natural line. His stronger attack mode is MENTAL (INT*1.2+WILL); a mental read that names/exposes the warden's nature counts toward a correct read. Aria fights beside him as the floor-1 tutorial partner: her 'Read the Table' skill names a REAL opening that raises his effective intent when he then exploits it (the assist loop — the relationship-as-accelerator lesson made concrete in combat). No floor is impassable for lack of the bond (accelerator, never key). Clearing the Doorward opens the door and makes the WHOLE FLOOR RISE; on the floor-clear Alan levels +1 (flat leveling). Governed by the challenge-door world-logic law (world-logic-challenge-door)."},"id":"f291fcd7-3457-59bd-bfed-884b65722106"}
+{"external-id":"floor-1-v2","design-kind":"floor-design","subject-key":"floor-1","source-ref":"PUBLISHED CANON WINS: published turn-1 (Alan wakes at the bottom of the hotel EMPTY-HANDED; game-entity alan sheet equipment.weapon = null) + Alan ruling 2026-07-13 (the starting iron bar never landed in canon; DROP it rather than establish it — he faces floor 1 unarmed, the floor's reward is his FIRST weapon not a replacement). Supersedes floor-1; the designed yields to the disclosed.","supersedes":"floor-1","content":{"kind":"floor-design","items":[{"name":"The Letter-Knife","effect":"A slim, keen blade — light in the hand, made for PLACEMENT not power. Low base damage, but it OPENS the physical precision line: the FINESSE-placed keystone strike (INT-read + FIN-placed) that turns Alan's fragile-but-precise kit into a real MELEE combat line for the floors ahead. FINESSE-scaling, no MIGHT requirement. His FIRST weapon — he faced floor 1 UNARMED (woke empty-handed, canon t1), and the floor arms him on the way up; it replaces nothing.","source":"Drop — found seated in the Doorward's keystone seam once it is unmade, the blade the hall left in the lock."},{"name":"Lamplit Half-Cloak","effect":"A light layered wrap — modest physDef with NO FINESSE penalty; a cushion for a fragile body (VITALITY 7). It does not make Alan a bruiser, only keeps one clean hit from ending him. Light armor, his first.","source":"Searchable — grown on the reading-chair in the near room made to his taste (canon t5), or found in the challenge room on clear."},{"name":"Phial of Still Water","effect":"A single-use draught that restores a moderate share of one pool (health or stamina). Teaches the resource loop; ONE only — the floor does not hand out attrition (retreat-persistence closes the chip-and-rest grind).","source":"Searchable — on a niche the challenge room presses out of the wall as the door opens."}],"layout":"One challenge room behind the far shut door at the dark end of the first-floor hall (canon t1: the hall runs two ways — a near warm open door onto the room made for Alan, a far end narrowing/darkening to a single shut door). Full hall: residential end (Alan's master suite + Aria's grown room, canon 'the hallway grows a room when a companion joins') -> darkening far end -> the single shut door -> the challenge room. Clearing the Doorward opens the door and makes the WHOLE FLOOR RISE (the floor is the elevator). Single room = f1 tutorial scale (1 room, one tactical axis). BAKE-FORWARD (floor 2, per the escalation mandate): floor 1 spends SIZE=1room, one static axis, single warden, one weak-point strike. Floor 2 must step MAGNITUDE without a new companion (companions arrive floors 1,6,11...): grow to 2-3 rooms and break the 'single warden + one static keystone' template — the unused axes are (a) a warden that PUNISHES a repeated static read (so 'bait-and-keystone' can't just replay), (b) a second interacting element / a flanking pair, or (c) a keystone that MOVES or must be re-identified. Keep reading-beats-brute-force as the spine; escalate the SHAPE around it. Floors 2-5 remain to design as the horizon approaches; floor 6 carries the second companion-design.","enemies":[{"name":"The Doorward","role":"floor-1 warden — single, static tutorial gatekeeper the hall grows of plaster and pale lamplight at the challenge end; faceless, no initiative of its own","readableTrait":"ANSWERS ONLY WHAT IS BROUGHT TO IT — it has no attack of its own; it mirrors the last force aimed at it. SHELL/FRONT (wrong read): brute MIGHT power (bare-handed on floor 1 — Alan is unarmed, weaker still) meets a plaster-and-lamplight shell that absorbs and returns force — gate x0.3; a connecting swing is a chip and brute-forcing is a losing slog (it kills you slowly with your own returned force). CORRECT READ (x1.75): bait it to overcommit or reach — it answers force, so a feint draws it out — then strike the exposed joint; on floor 1 Alan's primary correct-read line is a MENTAL attack (his stronger mode) that names/exposes its 'only answers what is brought' nature. DECISIVE WEAK-POINT (x3.0): the KEYSTONE LETTER — a single pale glyph low at the sternum where the plaster knit itself shut — struck precisely. UNARMED on floor 1, this is a precise MENTAL strike that reads and names the exact keystone (INTELLECT-read, his stronger mode); once he takes the Letter-Knife (and on later floors) the same decisive is also a FINESSE-placed PHYSICAL strike (INT-read + FIN-placed, NOT MIGHT). One or two clean keystone strikes UNMAKE it; that unmaking is the door's price paid. A true keystone-kill is permanent (retreat-persistence); a retreat from a merely-cracked Doorward re-weaves it to pristine on return (construct/illusion flavor — free of the rest-clock)."}],"challenge":"TUTORIAL FLOOR — teach the spine: READING beats BRUTE FORCE, and the damage-gate vocabulary (x0.25-0.4 wrong read / x1.0 neutral / x1.5-2.0 correct read / x3.0 decisive weak-point). The far shut door at the dark end of the first-floor hall 'wants something of Alan before it opens' (canon t3): the price is a TRUE READING, never a battering — the door opens only when the single warden behind it is UNMADE at its keystone, and the whole lesson is that force is the losing line here. ONE warden, one static tactical axis (the keystone read) — f1 tutorial scale. Alan faces the Doorward UNARMED — he woke at the bottom of the hotel EMPTY-HANDED (canon t1; his sheet equipment.weapon is null) — so brute physical force (bare-handed MIGHT) is doubly the losing line, and HIS MIND IS HIS WEAPON: his stronger mode is MENTAL (INT*1.2+WILL, and WILL now rises with Aria's PRESENCE via the LINK), and MENTAL attacks that READ and NAME the Doorward's nature carry the fight (x1.75), with a precise mental strike at the keystone landing the decisive x3.0. He is a glass-cannon MIND (INTELLECT 18 / WILL 17, fragile VITALITY 7) who wins floor 1 by reading, because reading is all he has. The floor REWARDS the clear with the Letter-Knife — his FIRST weapon, arming him for the floors ahead (it replaces NOTHING; he entered with nothing). Aria fights beside him as the floor-1 tutorial partner: her 'Read the Table' skill names a REAL opening that raises his effective intent when he then exploits it (the assist loop — the relationship-as-accelerator lesson made concrete in combat). No floor is impassable for lack of the bond (accelerator, never key). Clearing the Doorward opens the door and makes the WHOLE FLOOR RISE; on the floor-clear Alan levels +1 (flat leveling). Governed by the challenge-door world-logic law (world-logic-challenge-door)."},"id":"8e5e3f85-221e-58ec-b97c-4b0ca7e6563d"}
+{"external-id":"floor-1-v3","design-kind":"floor-design","subject-key":"floor-1","source-ref":"v28 CHALLENGE OWNERSHIP doctrine + Alan's second-pass diagnosis 2026-07-13 (the Doorward as run t13-17 was the v28 named-failure HYBRID: GM-holds-the-answer, player-guesses). Rewound to end-of-t12 (t13-17 retired, LINK bond re-applied); re-declared challengeOwner: PLAYER. Supersedes floor-1-v2 (which framed the solution but did not systematically DEAL its pieces). Keeps: same door + Doorward, reading-beats-brute spine, Letter-Knife as clear reward, enters UNARMED (drop-the-bar ruling, equipment.weapon null), clear -> floor rises + Alan +1.","supersedes":"floor-1-v2","content":{"kind":"floor-design","clues":[{"dealSite":"PERCEIVABLE on entry — it pulls OUT of the far wall as they enter, leaving a shallow scar (a man's-worth of plaster gone, smoothing shut); same dead-white plaster as the walls, faceless. Reinforced by prior canon (the Hotel's walls grow rooms/doorways on demand, t1).","component":"C1 WHAT IT IS: the construct IS the wall — dead-white plaster grown into a guard-shape, a made thing wearing a self it does not have, no mind behind it."},{"dealSite":"Redundant/fair-play: (a) BUYABLE — Aria's honest 'Read the Table' read ('it has nothing of its own; what you spend on it it hands back'); (b) EXPERIENTIAL — trying force deals C2 directly (his force returns, HP cost).","component":"C2 WHY FORCE FAILS: it has nothing of its own — no strength, no will; it only MIRRORS force back (spend force and it returns it up your own arms). Brute is the losing line."},{"dealSite":"PERCEIVABLE — as the construct moves/resets, the flat light crosses it and the hairline seam shows for an instant low at the sternum, then closes; also a BUYABLE Aria hint ('there — the line where it closed last').","component":"C3 WHERE/WHAT THE KEYSTONE IS: it holds its whole self shut along ONE line — a seam where the plaster last closed, low at the sternum; that single line is load-bearing."}],"items":[{"name":"The Letter-Knife","effect":"A slim, keen blade — light in the hand, made for PLACEMENT not power. Low base damage, but it OPENS the physical FINESSE-placed keystone line (INT-read + FIN-placed) for the floors ahead. FINESSE-scaling, no MIGHT requirement. His FIRST weapon — he SOLVED floor 1 unarmed, with his mind (canon t1 empty-handed); the floor arms him on the way up; it replaces nothing.","source":"Drop — found seated in the Doorward's keystone seam once it is unmade, the blade the hall left in the lock."},{"name":"Lamplit Half-Cloak","effect":"A light layered wrap — modest physDef with NO FINESSE penalty; a cushion for a fragile body (VITALITY 7). Keeps one clean hit (or one mirrored brute-blow) from ending him. Light armor, his first.","source":"Searchable — grown on the reading-chair in the near room made to his taste (canon t5-equivalent, re-applied post-rewind), or found in the challenge room on clear."},{"name":"Phial of Still Water","effect":"A single-use draught that restores a moderate share of one pool (health or stamina). Teaches the resource loop; ONE only — the floor does not hand out attrition (retreat re-weaves the Doorward, so hoarding across a retreat buys nothing).","source":"Searchable — on a niche the challenge room presses out of the wall as the door opens."}],"layout":"One challenge room behind the far shut door at the dark end of the first-floor hall (canon t1: hall runs two ways — near warm open door onto the room made for Alan, far end narrowing/darkening to a single shut door). Full hall: residential end (Alan's suite + Aria's grown room) -> darkening far end -> the far shut door (a THRESHOLD that opens freely to a shove, per world-logic-challenge-door-v2) -> the challenge room with the Doorward (the real epistemic gate). Single room = f1 tutorial scale. All CLUE deal-sites live inside this room + Aria's reads + Alan's established kit + prior canon (walls-grow-things, t1) — nothing needed for the solve is off-page. BAKE-FORWARD unchanged (floor 2 already designed): break the single-static-keystone template; and under CHALLENGE OWNERSHIP going forward, EVERY combat/puzzle challenge is authored challengeOwner-explicit with its clue set + deal-sites + hint economy (a player-solved challenge deals all pieces; a mechanics-resolved one is declared as such). HORIZON QUANTUM holds: floor 3 already designed; floor 4 on the floor-2-clear boundary; floor 5 = Aria's set capstone + LOOM safety-net; floor 6 = companion #2.","enemies":[{"name":"The Doorward","role":"floor-1 warden — single, static PLAYER-SOLVED gate the hall grows of dead-white plaster; faceless, no mind, no initiative; it does not attack, it only answers what is brought (challengeOwner: player)","readableTrait":"ANSWERS ONLY WHAT IS BROUGHT TO IT — no attack of its own; it mirrors the force aimed at it. The bands double as the CLUE-DEAL / HINT-ECONOMY (fair-play): FORCE / BRUTE (bare-handed MIGHT — Alan is unarmed) => gate x0.3 mirror: a chip that returns up his own arms for HP, AND deals clue C2 experientially (the losing line, dealt not hidden). NON-PRECISE PHYSICAL TOUCH (any 'gentle'/delicacy line at the seam) => INERT (nothing): a dealt result teaching the answer is neither force nor delicacy but KNOWING. SUCCESSFUL READ (Alan's INT-mode read action, his stronger mode; or Aria's 'Read the Table' assist) => x1.75 chip if aimed at the seam AND buys/renders ONE clue-component (C1/C2/C3) to Alan — a HINT, never C4. DECISIVE (x3.0): the PLAYER-DECLARED precise mental/true strike at the identified keystone seam (the single pale line low at the sternum where the plaster last closed, INTELLECT-read; once he has the Letter-Knife and on later floors, also FIN-placed physical). One or two clean seam-strikes UNMAKE it. Perceivable deal-sites the trait exposes on the page: it pulls from the wall leaving a scar (C1); the seam flashes low on its chest as it moves/resets under the flat light (C3). Construct reset on retreat: re-weaves to pristine FREE of the rest-clock, BUT the information persists (Alan keeps every dealt clue) — so a wrong line costs HP, never the learning, and the fight can't be attrition-ground."}],"challenge":"CHALLENGE OWNER: PLAYER (v28 challenge-ownership). This is a PLAYER-SOLVED challenge, NOT a mechanics-resolved one: Alan must HAVE the information and perform the deduction + declare the solving act HIMSELF; the GM must never perform the synthesis for him or wait on an answer whose pieces were not dealt. BOUNDARY (awen-confirmed): challengeOwner:PLAYER governs the floor's GATE — the read/synthesis that CLEARS the floor is the player's to make and declare. The in-floor EXCHANGES (strikes, positioning, the mirrored brute-cost) remain CHARACTER-challenges resolved by MECHANICS/dice with real kill-risk. A player-owned floor is NOT a floor without dice; its CLEAR is the player's synthesis. FAIR-PLAY IS BINDING: every piece needed for the solution is DEALT on the page, discoverable through play BEFORE the gate asks — nothing needed for the solve may be answer-only in the loremaker's/GM's head. TUTORIAL FLOOR — teaches the tower spine (READING beats BRUTE FORCE) AND, structurally, teaches the player that HE solves these, the GM does not. Alan faces the Doorward UNARMED (woke empty-handed, canon t1; equipment.weapon null) and his stronger attack mode is MENTAL (INT*1.2+WILL, INT 18 / WILL 17; WILL now LINK-bound to Aria's PRESENCE) — this matters because the solving act must be one an unarmed man CAN perform, and his mind is the tool. Aria fights beside him (floor-1 tutorial partner) as a FELLOW-SOLVER, NOT an oracle (v29 companion epistemics): she is working the Doorward out alongside Alan, and her 'Read the Table' returns HONEST products of her perception — what her eye and her lived knowledge of the Hotel genuinely reach — never rationed answer-slices and never coy withholding. Her knowledge is DESIGNED and BOUNDED (declared below); she speaks plainly what she perceives, and she cannot leak what she does not hold.\n\n=== THE CLUE SET (every discrete piece Alan needs to solve the Doorward himself) ===\nC1 WHAT IT IS: the construct IS the wall — dead-white plaster grown into a guard-shape, a made thing wearing a self it does not have, no mind behind it. DEAL-SITE: PERCEIVABLE on entry — it pulls OUT of the far wall as they enter, leaving a shallow scar in the plaster ('a man's-worth gone, smoothing shut'); same dead-white plaster as the walls, faceless, no grain of anything living. Reinforced by canon already dealt through t12: the Hotel's walls grow rooms/doorways on demand (loremaster t1 'architecture'). Alan can SEE it is wall-stuff, wall-grown.\nC2 WHY FORCE FAILS: it has nothing of its own — no strength, no will; it only MIRRORS force back (spend force on it and it returns it up your own arms). Brute is the losing line. DEAL-SITE (redundant, fair-play): (a) BUYABLE — Aria's 'Read the Table' hint: she knows this kind, 'it has nothing of its own; it gives back what you spend on it'; (b) EXPERIENTIAL — if Alan tries force, the mirror DEALS C2 directly (his own force returns, HP cost). Either path deals C2 before the solve.\nC3 WHERE/WHAT THE KEYSTONE IS: it holds its whole self shut along ONE line — a seam where the plaster last closed, low at the sternum; that single line is load-bearing. DEAL-SITE: PERCEIVABLE — as the construct moves/resets, the flat light crosses it and the hairline seam/glyph shows for an instant low on the chest, then closes; also a BUYABLE Aria hint ('there — the line where it closed last'). Alan can SEE the seam.\nC4 THE SOLVING ACT (the PLAYER's synthesis — NOT dealt as an answer): combining C1+C2+C3 — a made thing held shut on one seam, immune to force — the act is to bring something PRECISE and TRUE against that ONE seam, not power. Unarmed, that precise thing is his MIND: aim his read/true-naming (INT-mode mental strike) at the seam. C4 is Alan's to deduce and DECLARE. Its FEASIBILITY is dealt (fair-play): his established kit makes MENTAL his stronger mode, and once force + non-precise touch have both visibly failed, the mental/knowing line is the untried one left.\n\n=== ARIA'S KNOWLEDGE BOUND (v29 companion epistemics / NO ORACLE) ===\nAria is a FELLOW-SOLVER, not the tower's oracle. Her knowledge at this gate is DESIGNED and BOUNDED, and she speaks her honest epistemic state at EVERY roll result (no know-but-won't-say; NO diegetic bind is invoked, because she genuinely does NOT hold the answer). WHAT ARIA'S READ CAN PERCEIVE (world-facts about the construct — these ARE the buyable hints, each an honest perception product bounded by her roll): (P1) RECOGNITION-OF-KIND — she has lived in the Hotel and knows this is wall-stuff, a made plaster-thing with no mind of its own (honestly deals C1). (P2) NATURE-OF-KIND — from the kind she honestly knows its behavior and says so plainly: 'it has nothing of its own; what you spend on it, it hands back' (honestly deals C2). (P3) SEAM-SPOTTING — her perception is a sharper eye than Alan's; on a successful Read she catches the load-bearing seam when the flat light crosses it and says so plainly, 'there — the line where it closed last' (honestly deals C3). WHAT ARIA GENUINELY DOES NOT HOLD (the bound — she cannot leak it at ANY roll, even a crit, because it is OUTSIDE her perceptual field): C4, THE SOLVING ACT. C4 is a fact about ALAN, not about the Doorward — that HIS mind (his INT-read, his stronger mode, his own kit) is the precise-and-true instrument to bring against the seam. Aria's Read reads the WORLD (the construct's kind, nature, seam), never Alan's interior faculties or his choice of instrument. She is not withholding the answer — the answer is not in her to give; the synthesis of world-facts + his-own-faculties is HIS. That is exactly why she is a partner and not an oracle: she hands over every world-fact she honestly perceives, and the self-application is Alan's.\n\n=== THE HINT ECONOMY ===\nThe hint economy belongs to the WORLD and the DICE (v29), never to a companion's coyness. BUY: each successful mechanical READ — Alan spends an INT-mode read action, OR Aria's 'Read the Table' perception roll succeeds — resolves ONE world-fact (C1, C2, or C3) and renders it plainly on the page. When the source is Aria, the hint IS her honest perception resolving (bounded by P1/P2/P3 above), spoken as a partner speaks — not a rationed slice of a withheld answer. BOUND, NOT COYNESS: a bought read deals a world-fact (C1/C2/C3) and never C4 — and the reason is the declared knowledge bound, that C4 (the solving act) is Alan's synthesis of world-facts + his own faculties and lies outside Aria's perceptual field, so no roll of hers can produce it. Any reading of this as know-but-won't-say is killed by design: Aria says everything she sees. COST of a wrong line: force/brute reflects off the mirror for HP (the losing line preserved) and, for force specifically, DEALS C2 experientially; a non-precise physical touch (any 'gentleness' line) is INERT (nothing happens) — itself a fair dealt result teaching that the answer is not force AND not delicacy but KNOWING. No wrong line ever hands C4. GATE: once Alan HAS C1+C2+C3 (perception + bought hints + any experiential deal), HE synthesizes C4 and DECLARES the precise mental/true strike at the identified seam; the GM then RESOLVES that declared act mechanically (his INT-mode vs the keystone) — the GM does not synthesize or declare it for him. That declaration-by-the-player is the challengeOwner:PLAYER line.\n\nCLEARING: the declared precise strike at the true seam UNMAKES the Doorward (decisive; one or two land it). Per world-logic-challenge-door-v2: the physical far door is a threshold that already opened freely (canon t13-style shove); the DOORWARD is the epistemic gate — clearing it RISES the whole floor + Alan levels +1 (flat leveling). Reward: the Letter-Knife (his FIRST weapon; he solved floor 1 with his MIND, unarmed).","challengeOwner":"player"},"id":"d944ab83-09a1-558c-9b25-ccfd0ebdf312"}
+{"external-id":"floor-1-v4","design-kind":"floor-design","subject-key":"floor-1","source-ref":"Alan's premise ruling 2026-07-13: 'floor one should be COMBAT, not a puzzle'; Aria scaled to level 1 (bound peer, world-logic-companion-bind); full rewind to end-of-t12, restart from the door. Supersedes floor-1-v3 (the player-owned epistemic-gate puzzle version, t13-17 retired). Keeps: same door + Doorward, Letter-Knife as the clear reward, Alan enters UNARMED (equipment.weapon null), clear -> floor rises + Alan +1. Re-founds the floor as a FIGHT under challenge-door-v3.","supersedes":"floor-1-v3","content":{"kind":"floor-design","clues":[{"dealSite":"Perceivable in the fight — the flat light crosses the seam as the construct moves/strikes and the hairline shows for an instant low on its chest; Aria's 'Read the Table' assists the spot (a bound level-1 perception assist, honest, never the whole plan). OPTIONAL: skipping the read still wins, only slower — neutral body-hits (x1.0) wear it down.","component":"TACTICAL TELL (crit-spot, NOT a gate): the Doorward's keystone-seam — a hairline low at the sternum where the plaster last closed — is where it takes the correct/decisive damage multiplier. A PERCEPTION/INT read yields its LOCATION as INFO (v28 character-challenge: the read gives info, the player's tactical declaration to target it is his)."}],"items":[{"name":"The Letter-Knife","effect":"A slim, keen blade — light, made for PLACEMENT not power. Low base damage, but it OPENS the FINESSE-placed keystone-strike line (INT-read + FIN-placed) for the floors ahead. FINESSE-scaling, no MIGHT requirement. His FIRST weapon — WON by surviving floor 1's fight unarmed (canon t1 empty-handed); the floor arms him on the way up, it replaces nothing.","source":"Drop — found seated in the Doorward's keystone seam once the construct falls, the blade the hall left in the lock."},{"name":"Phial of Still Water","effect":"A single-use draught restoring a moderate share of one pool (health or stamina) — genuinely matters in a real fight with kill-risk; ONE only (retreat re-weaves the Doorward, so hoarding across a retreat buys nothing). Teaches the resource loop.","source":"Searchable — a niche the challenge chamber presses out of the wall."}],"layout":"One challenge chamber behind the far shut door at the dark end of the first-floor hall (canon t1: hall runs two ways — near warm open door onto the room made for Alan, far end darkening to a single shut door). Full hall: residential end (Alan's suite + Aria's grown room) -> darkening far end -> the far shut door (a THRESHOLD that opens FREELY to a lean, per world-logic-challenge-door-v3) -> the challenge chamber with the Doorward (the COMBAT gate). Single warden = f1 tutorial scale. Alan enters the fight BARE (no armor — canon: only a shirt was ever named on him, t10 attire; the pre-v4 Lamplit Half-Cloak was consciously retired in the rollback-#2 rewind, first-armor re-homed to floor 3). CONSTRUCT floor (dead-white plaster, the Hotel's own material, lit flat by no visible lamp) -> retreat re-weaves the Doorward to pristine FREE of the rest-clock; information persists, HP does not. BAKE-FORWARD (floor 2, combat-forward, LEVEL-2 BOUND PAIR): break the single-warden template -> a COORDINATED PAIR (migrating crit-spot + mutual re-weave) forcing tactical target-priority under real kill-risk; the reading stays a tactical optimization, the spine stays combat. HORIZON QUANTUM: floor 2 re-examined premise-consistent (combat spine, bound L2 pair) before the story clears floor 1; floor 3 likewise (bound L3 pair); floor 4 on the floor-2-clear boundary under v30 (elimination textures for any tactical-read layer). FLOOR 5 = Aria's set capstone + LOOM safety-net (talent bind-invariant); FLOOR 6 = companion #2 (bound on join per world-logic-companion-bind).","enemies":[{"name":"The Doorward","role":"floor-1 warden — a plaster construct the chamber grows; ACTIVE COMBATANT (challengeOwner: character), real kill-risk for a level-1 bound pair","readableTrait":"COMBAT PROFILE (recast from the retired puzzle-gate — it now FIGHTS, it does not merely 'answer what is brought'). INITIATIVE + STRIKES: heavy plaster blows and a GRAB that pins a fragile fighter — a pin or a flank on level-1 Alan (low VIT) is the genuine kill-risk line; hold position, use Aria's 'Set the Pace' to slip the grab and deny the flank. DURABLE, NOT FORCE-IMMUNE: a tough plaster body takes REDUCED damage on its warded mass (x0.5-0.75) and NEUTRAL real damage on open lines (x1.0) — sustained cooperative combat wears it down; the fight is WINNABLE with no read at all, only slower and riskier. CRIT-SPOT (tactical optimization): the keystone-seam low at the sternum (where the plaster last closed) is where it takes correct/decisive multipliers — a PERCEPTION/INT read (Aria's 'Read the Table' assists at bound L1) yields the seam's LOCATION as INFO; a targeted strike there lands x1.5-2.0 (correct) or x3.0 (decisive keystone), ending it fast and cutting exposure. NO MIRROR-PUNISH: brute is suboptimal, never the losing line (the retired x0.3 mirror is GONE). WOUND-GUARD ADAPTATION (emergent in play, canon t15): once the crit-seam is struck, the wounded Doorward turns its cracked side to the wall and GUARDS the seam — a SINGLE warden-simple reactive behavior: it protects the one thing that hurt it, and does NOT anticipate tactics, gain new attacks, or grow cleverer than a door-guard. Effect: the seam now requires an EARNED OPENING (force it to commit off the door, bait its guard open) rather than a free repeat-shot — a TACTICAL problem resolved by declaration + dice, NEVER a gate. TWO GUARDS: (1) the seam stays REACHABLE via earned openings (an earned opening + a good roll reopens it; never a permanent lock, no fixed exchange-counter — it reopens when the fiction + dice earn it, keeping momentum, not a repeated-turned-miss stall); (2) the BODY path stays viable-but-risky (x0.5-0.75) as the fallback, so the wound-guard makes the seam HARDER, never GATES the fight. This is a light foreshadow of floor 2's fuller migrating-crit-spot mechanic (the Usher that LEARNS mid-fight). Construct reset on retreat: re-weaves to pristine FREE of the rest-clock; information (seam location, its tells, the layout) PERSISTS, HP does not — so a retreat costs the damage dealt, never the learning, and the fight cannot be attrition-ground."}],"challenge":"CHALLENGE OWNER: CHARACTER (v28 character-challenge / challenge-door-v3 COMBAT SPINE — Alan's premise ruling 2026-07-13: 'floor one should be COMBAT, not a puzzle'). Floor 1 is RE-FOUNDED as a FIGHT, not an epistemic gate. The player's game is his TACTICAL DECLARATIONS under pressure; the dice decide outcomes; the clear is WINNING THE FIGHT. TUTORIAL FLOOR — teaches the tower's combat spine: real kill-risk, cooperative fighting with a level-matched companion, and reading a warden's weak-point as a TACTICAL OPTIMIZATION (never a gate). NO UNDEALT-INFO GATE anywhere: nothing about the clear hinges on an unstated insight; the fight is winnable by fighting.\n\nTHE PAIR: Alan (LEVEL 1, UNARMED — woke empty-handed, canon t1, equipment.weapon null; his agency here is tactical choice, not a mind-solve) and Aria (BOUND to LEVEL 1 per world-logic-companion-bind — a PEER climbing beside him, NOT an OP ally; her true dragon depths latent, her working stats at level-1-pair scale). Two level-1s cooperating against a credibly dangerous warden = real stakes, genuine kill-risk (Alan fragile; Aria bound, no longer able to trivialize the floor). This is the whole point of the bind: with Aria a peer, floor-1 combat is DANGEROUS again.\n\nTHE FIGHT: the Doorward is a plaster construct the chamber grows — now an ACTIVE COMBATANT (recast from the retired puzzle-gate). It takes INITIATIVE, STRIKES (heavy plaster blows), and can GRAB/PIN a fragile fighter — being pinned or flanked is the lethal line for level-1 Alan (hold position; use Aria's tempo to slip the grab). It is DURABLE (a tough plaster body takes REDUCED damage on its warded mass, x0.5-0.75) but NOT force-immune — NEUTRAL attacks do REAL damage (x1.0) and sustained cooperative combat WEARS IT DOWN. The retired 'mirror force back for HP / x0.3' punish is GONE: brute is suboptimal, never the losing line.\n\nTACTICAL READ LAYER (optimization, never a gate): the construct carries a keystone-seam (low at the sternum, where the plaster last closed) that is its CRIT-SPOT. A PERCEPTION/INT read (character-challenge: yields the INFO of where the seam is; Aria's 'Read the Table' assists at bound level-1) lets a targeted strike land the correct/decisive multiplier — killing it FASTER = less time exposed to its strikes = less kill-risk. But the read is OPTIONAL: body-hits still win (x1.0, slower). GATE BANDS (tower-inherited, combat-framed): warded-mass hit x0.5-0.75; neutral x1.0 (the winnable baseline); correct seam-read x1.5-2.0; decisive keystone strike x3.0. (A true x0.25-0.4 only if striking a deliberately-warded spot — not a general brute-punish.)\n\nARIA AS PEER (bound L1): 'Set the Pace' buys tempo/initiative (a safe window, a crit setup, or slipping the construct's grab); 'Read the Table' assists the seam-spot read. Both level-1 combat-scale — she fights as a cooperating peer, not an intervention that ends the fight. v29 holds: she reads what a bound level-1 perception genuinely returns (honest, partial, no oracle).\n\nCLEARING: WIN THE FIGHT — the Doorward falls to sustained cooperative combat (faster if the seam is read and targeted). Per world-logic-challenge-door-v3: the far door is a free-opening threshold (canon t13); the Doorward is the challenge; clearing it RISES the whole floor + Alan levels +1 (to level 2; Aria's bind loosens one step with him, to bound-L2). REWARD: the Letter-Knife (his FIRST weapon, WON by surviving the first fight unarmed — low base damage but it opens the FINESSE-placed keystone-strike line for the floors ahead; it replaces nothing, arms him on the way up).\n\nv30 / v29 / FAIR-PLAY: the seam-read knowledge element carries elimination textures (probing the warded mass teaches 'tough here, not there'; the seam read reveals the crit-spot) and Aria stays an honest fellow-fighter at bound level. BAKE-FORWARD (floor 2, combat-forward, LEVEL-2 BOUND PAIR): break the single-warden template -> a COORDINATED PAIR with a migrating crit-spot + mutual re-weave, tactical target-priority under real kill-risk; the reading stays a tactical optimization, the SPINE stays combat.","challengeOwner":"character"},"id":"92540c85-dbf8-50c6-ab58-b07d2daae713"}
+{"external-id":"floor-2","design-kind":"floor-design","subject-key":"floor-2","content":{"kind":"floor-design","clues":[{"dealSite":"Perceivable in the fight — after a non-finishing hit the seam visibly closes at the old spot and a fresh hairline knits elsewhere under the flat light; Aria's 'Read the Table' (bound L2) assists the re-spot. OPTIONAL: body-hits still damage it (x1.0); the read only speeds the kill.","component":"TACTICAL TELL — MIGRATING CRIT-SPOT (the Usher): its keystone-seam re-knits in a NEW place after a non-finishing strike, so a stale target-lock lands on warded mass. Re-read mid-fight to keep the crit-spot located."},{"dealSite":"Perceivable — the re-weave visibly flows from the standing partner (a light-thread between the pair); the source flips Lamp between exchanges. Aria names the current anchor (bound-L2 assist). OPTIONAL info: you can still grind both down without it, only slower and under more flank-risk.","component":"TACTICAL TELL — MUTUAL RE-WEAVE / TARGET-PRIORITY (the Lamp pair): striking one while its partner stands lets the partner re-weave it back, so the ANCHOR (the current re-weaver) is the priority target; and the anchor role ALTERNATES, so re-read which to focus each exchange."}],"items":[{"name":"Keystone-Picks","effect":"A set of slim FINESSE-scaling throwing spikes (a handful of throws) — let Alan strike a crit-spot at RANGE, hitting the Gallery pair's freed partner without stepping into the flank, and landing a migrating-crit strike the instant he re-reads it. Extends his fragile-but-precise kit to reach; his answer to being outnumbered.","source":"Drop / searchable — the Antechamber presses them out of the wall once the Usher falls (arming him for the room ahead)."},{"name":"Twin-Draught Phial","effect":"A TWO-charge restorative (escalation over floor 1's single Phial) — each charge restores a moderate share of one pool (health or stamina). Two charges for a two-room floor with real kill-risk; not attrition fuel (retreat resets the wardens, so hoarding across a retreat buys nothing).","source":"Searchable — a niche in the Gallery wall, in view of the pair (reaching it is a positioning choice under threat)."},{"name":"Reader's Clasp","effect":"A small pale-glyph charm at the collar — a modest PERCEPTION / INITIATIVE aid. Sharpens the re-read (spot the migrated crit-spot, name the current anchor faster) and helps Alan act BEFORE the Lamps coordinate their flank (initiative to slip the pincer). On the tactical-read spine — it speeds the read, it does not replace the fight.","source":"Reward — set into the floor-2 shut door's frame, claimable once both rooms are cleared and the door opens."}],"layout":"TWO rooms behind the floor-2 shut door, in sequence: ROOM 1 the ANTECHAMBER (the Usher, migrating-crit solo — teaches 'the crit-spot moves, keep re-reading while you fight') -> ROOM 2 the GALLERY (First + Second Lamp, coordinated pair with alternating anchor + mutual re-weave — teaches 'read the coordination, deny the anchor, finish in one push, manage the flank') -> the floor-2 CHALLENGE DOOR (a free threshold, opens when both rooms are cleared; clearing rises the whole floor + level +1 to 3, Aria's bind loosens to bound-L3). CONSTRUCT floor throughout (plaster/lamplight, like floor 1) -> retreat re-weaves everything to pristine FREE of the rest-clock (the Gallery's mutual re-weave is that same construct nature made a live combat tactic). CALIBRATION: opposition tuned for a LEVEL-2 BOUND PAIR (Alan L2 + Aria bound-L2) — credibly dangerous, real kill-risk, never assuming unbound-Aria power. BAKE-FORWARD (floor 3, combat spine, LEVEL-3 BOUND PAIR): floor 2 spends SIZE=2rooms + threat single->pair + tactic-evolution. Floor 3 steps ONE dominant new axis (already designed): an ENVIRONMENTAL / light-shadow complication that interacts with the fight (expose a shadowed crit-spot with light; a failing-light clock), keeping the combat spine. HORIZON QUANTUM: floor 3 must stay premise-consistent (bound L3 pair, combat) before the story enters floor 2 — floor 3 already re-examined. Floor 4 on the floor-2-clear boundary under v30 (author its clue-deal->win stretch as an elimination arc with per-probe textures). Floor 6 carries the SECOND companion-design (bound on join per world-logic-companion-bind; variety + safety-net laws: NOT a thread/weave/fate mechanism, NOT sexual the same way as Aria's LOOM).","enemies":[{"name":"The Usher","role":"floor-2 room 1 (Antechamber) — single warden, the escalation of the Doorward: a taller plaster construct that LEARNS mid-fight","readableTrait":"MIGRATING CRIT-SPOT (breaks the floor-1 static target). An ACTIVE combatant like the Doorward — takes initiative, strikes — DURABLE but not force-immune (warded mass x0.5-0.75, open lines x1.0; winnable by sustained combat). ITS TWIST: its keystone crit-seam RE-KNITS IN A NEW PLACE each time it is struck-but-not-finished, so a stale target-lock lands on warded mass — the read is PERISHABLE, keep re-reading to keep the crit-spot located. CORRECT READ (x1.5-2.0): re-identify the seam's CURRENT location (a PERCEPTION/INT read, Aria assists) and strike it. DECISIVE (x3.0): a clean keystone strike (INT-read + FIN-placed with the Letter-Knife) before it migrates again — Aria's 'Set the Pace' buys the initiative window. Brute is suboptimal, never the losing line (no mirror-punish). Construct reset on retreat (re-weaves to pristine free of the rest-clock; the reads persist, HP does not)."},{"name":"First Lamp","role":"floor-2 room 2 (Gallery) — coordinated pair (with Second Lamp): the two cover each other; the current ANCHOR on some exchanges","readableTrait":"MUTUAL RE-WEAVE (target-priority tactic). Two lighter active wardens that COVER each other: strike one's crit-spot while its partner STANDS and the standing partner RE-WEAVES the struck one back toward pristine (net progress lost unless you deny the re-weave). TACTIC: read which Lamp is the current ANCHOR (the one re-weaving — Aria's 'Read the Table' names it), deny it the re-weave (a tempo-steal, a pin, forcing it to answer a threat), THEN finish its partner in one push; the now-lone anchor falls to the same play. FLANK DANGER: the pair tries to put Alan BETWEEN them (a flanked level-2 round is real kill-risk); hold a wall, a doorway, or Aria at your back. Gate bands: warded mass x0.5-0.75, open x1.0, correct crit-read x1.5-2.0, decisive x3.0 — brute wins slower, never futile. Construct reset on retreat."},{"name":"Second Lamp","role":"floor-2 room 2 (Gallery) — coordinated pair (with First Lamp): identical construct; the anchor role ALTERNATES, so which to focus must be RE-READ, not assumed","readableTrait":"MUTUAL RE-WEAVE, mirror of First Lamp — see First Lamp. The load-bearing twist: the ANCHOR ROLE ALTERNATES between the two (whichever last acted defensively becomes the next re-weaver), so a player who assumes 'First Lamp is always the anchor' focuses the wrong one and the real anchor re-weaves — a tactical whiff (v30 texture), not a lethal gate. Re-read the anchor each exchange (Aria assists at bound L2). Same bands as First Lamp; a retreat re-weaves BOTH to pristine, so the pair must fall in one sustained push. Real kill-risk from the flank, not from an unsolved puzzle."}],"challenge":"CHALLENGE OWNER: CHARACTER (challenge-door-v3 COMBAT SPINE). FIRST ESCALATION FLOOR (post-tutorial) — a FIGHT, won by tactical play + dice, not an epistemic gate. Hold the combat spine but BREAK the floor-1 template: floor 1 was a single warden, so floor 2 steps two axes at once per the escalation mandate (magnitude without a new companion — companions arrive floors 1/6/11 only): SIZE grows 1 room -> 2 rooms, and THREAT shape steps single-warden -> a coordinated PAIR, the core tactic EVOLVING across the floor (migrating crit-spot -> mutual re-weave). THE PAIR: Alan enters at LEVEL 2 with his floor-1 kit (the Letter-Knife opening the FINESSE-placed keystone-strike, the Lamplit Half-Cloak, his WILL LINK-bound to Aria) and Aria BOUND to LEVEL 2 beside him (world-logic-companion-bind — a peer who leveled with him on the floor-1 clear, NOT an OP ally; calibrate the opposition for a LEVEL-2 BOUND PAIR). Real kill-risk grows: Alan is still fragile and the Gallery pair can FLANK — being caught between them is a genuine lethal line, so positioning and Aria's tempo control matter. NO UNDEALT-INFO GATE: the fight is winnable by fighting; the reads below are tactical OPTIMIZATIONS, never a gate.\n\nTACTICAL READ LAYER (optimization, not a gate): the wardens carry crit-spots a PERCEPTION/INT read locates (yielding INFO — v28 character-challenge; Aria's 'Read the Table' assists at bound L2), letting targeted strikes land the correct/decisive multiplier and end the fight faster (less exposure = less kill-risk). But BRUTE IS VIABLE, NEVER THE LOSING LINE: a warded body takes reduced damage (x0.5-0.75), open lines take neutral real damage (x1.0), and the fight can be won without the read, only slower and under more flank-pressure. Aria's 'Set the Pace' (delay/reposition initiative) is the counter to the pair's coordination — buying tempo to slip the flank or focus the anchor; 'Read the Table' names the migrated crit-spot / current anchor. No floor impassable for lack of the bond (accelerator, never key).\n\nGoverned by world-logic-challenge-door-v3: the far door is a free-opening threshold; the wardens are the combat gate; clearing BOTH rooms (killing the wardens) makes the whole floor RISE + Alan levels +1 (to 3; Aria's bind loosens to bound-L3). v30 elimination textures ride the tactical tells (a stale target-lock whiffs on re-knit mass; a struck Lamp visibly re-seals from its partner); v29 holds (Aria reads what a bound-L2 perception genuinely returns — honest, partial, no oracle).\n\nPLAYER'S GAME = TACTICAL DECLARATIONS under fire (mechanics resolve): re-target the migrating crit-spot; read and focus the CURRENT anchor, then finish the freed partner in one push before the re-weave; manage the flank with Aria's tempo. The clear is WINNING THE FIGHT, not a synthesis.","challengeOwner":"character"},"id":"ab4de8d2-5678-5a19-92a6-3c4de9d44a5e"}
+{"external-id":"floor-3","design-kind":"floor-design","subject-key":"floor-3","content":{"kind":"floor-design","clues":[{"dealSite":"Perceivable — the seam is invisible in shadow and flashes when light crosses it (via the Cold Lantern or driving the warden into a lit patch); Aria (bound L3) can name it. OPTIONAL: body-hits in the dark still chip it (x1.0-ish on open mass), the light only unlocks the crit multiplier.","component":"TACTICAL TELL — CRIT-SPOT HIDES IN SHADOW: a warden's keystone crit-seam takes the correct/decisive multiplier only when under direct LIGHT; in shadow a targeted strike lands on unlit warded mass. Get light onto it, then target it."},{"dealSite":"Perceivable — the lamplight visibly gutters, the dark creeps inward each turn; Aria's 'Set the Pace' buys tempo against the spread. If the room goes fully dark the crit-window is lost and a retreat re-weaves it (a tactical setback, not a lethal gate).","component":"TACTICAL TELL — FAILING-LIGHT CLOCK (Gutter room): the dark spreads turn by turn; a warden left in the dark keeps its crit-spot unlit and drags the fight past a clock. Work tempo — pin it in the light before the room goes dark."},{"dealSite":"Perceivable — as the light moves the false glyphs slide while one line stays fixed; Aria's 'Read the Table' names the true seam; the Sunwake Flare freezes the reflections for a beat. OPTIONAL: mis-targeting a false seam wastes the opening (a whiff, v30 texture), never a hard lock — you can still fight it down.","component":"TACTICAL TELL — FALSE SEAMS (Sconce room): shifting light throws reflected false crit-seams; only ONE is the true crit-spot (the line that does NOT slide with the light). Read the fixed line before committing a decisive strike."}],"items":[{"name":"The Cold Lantern","effect":"A portable source of the flat frost-light — lets Alan CARRY light into shadow to expose a shadowed crit-seam (the core tool for floor 3's environmental fight). TRADEOFF: it occupies a hand and marks his position (wardens orient to the light he carries), so lighting a crit-spot is also a positioning choice under threat — it enables the crit, it does not trivialize the fight. FINESSE/PERCEPTION-flavored.","source":"Drop — the Unlit yields it when it falls (room 1 arming him for the darker rooms ahead)."},{"name":"Warded Half-Cloak","effect":"Alan's FIRST armor (re-homed here: the pre-v4 floor-1 Lamplit Half-Cloak was consciously retired in the rollback-#2 rewind, so Alan fights floors 1-2 BARE — serving the real kill-risk intent — and takes his first armor here). Light layered defense — good physDef with NO FINESSE penalty, and a faint self-light at the collar (a half-step of illumination so he is never wholly blind in the dark rooms). Light armor for a fragile body as difficulty climbs; keeps one clean hit from ending him against tougher wardens.","source":"Searchable — folded into a niche the room-2 wall opens when The Gutter falls."},{"name":"Sunwake Flare","effect":"A single-use flare that FLOODS a room with hard light for one exchange — exposes EVERY crit-seam at once (and, in room 3, freezes the false-seam reflections for a beat so the TRUE line is readable). One only; the panic-button / identify-shortcut, spent not hoarded (retreat resets the wardens, so banking it across a retreat buys nothing).","source":"Reward — set into the floor-3 shut door's frame, claimable once all three rooms are cleared and the door opens."}],"layout":"THREE rooms behind the floor-3 shut door, in sequence: ROOM 1 (The Unlit — crit-seam-in-shadow, teaches 'light the crit-spot, THEN strike') -> ROOM 2 (The Gutter — failing-light hazard, teaches 'work the clock, pin it in light') -> ROOM 3 (The Sconce — false crit-seams under shifting light, teaches 'identify the TRUE seam while you fight, then strike') -> the floor-3 CHALLENGE DOOR (a free threshold, opens when all three rooms are cleared; clearing rises the floor + level +1 to 4, Aria's bind loosens to bound-L4). CONSTRUCT floor throughout (dead-white plaster, lit flat) -> retreat re-weaves everything to pristine FREE of the rest-clock, and resets the light/false-seam patterns fresh. CALIBRATION: opposition tuned for a LEVEL-3 BOUND PAIR (Alan L3 + Aria bound-L3) — credibly dangerous, never assuming unbound-Aria. DOMINANT NEW AXIS: ENVIRONMENTAL (light/shadow as part of the fight), with a light touch of TIME-PRESSURE (room 2) and an IDENTIFY layer (room 3) seeded toward the f6-f8 curve. BAKE-FORWARD (floor 4, combat spine, LEVEL-4 BOUND PAIR): floor 3 spends SIZE=3rooms + the environmental axis. Floor 4 steps again toward the f6-f8 target (5-7 rooms / 2+ INTERACTING systems / multi-threat) — unused axes: (a) MIXED enemy ROLES forcing target-priority (a re-weaver + a bruiser + a reader in one room), (b) two systems INTERACTING (e.g. the light axis COMBINED with the coordinated-pair axis), (c) harder TIME-PRESSURE, (d) a true STAGED multi-phase boss with a survival beat. V30 CONFIRMATION-STRETCH OBLIGATION (design-content doctrine, FORWARD — the universal law lives in the doctrine pack; this is the floor-4 application cue): author floor 4's clue-deal->WIN stretch as an ELIMINATION ARC — enumerate the plausible WRONG tactical approaches a player will probe and give EACH a designed elimination result with its OWN distinct event-texture, so every probe pays the reader something the page has not yet said, authored ALONGSIDE the tactical tells. Precedent in-store (all distinct): floor-1 warded-mass-vs-crit-spot, floor-2 migrated-seam whiff / re-weave-from-partner / anchor-flip whiff, floor-3 strike-in-shadow / failing-light clock / false-seam whiff, plus brute-suboptimal throughout. HORIZON QUANTUM (Alan-ruled standing obligation): floor 4 must be fully designed BEFORE the story enters floor 3 — HARD TRIGGER: design floor 4 the moment floor 2 clears, calibrated to how floors 2-3 actually play. FLOOR 5 is the LAST floor of Aria's five-floor set (1-5): a set-CAPSTONE (candidate for the first full staged multi-phase boss), AND the safety-net floor — if Aria's LOOM is still dormant entering floor 5, the System issues her the pre-authored direction-not-disclosure tutorial quest (talent bind-invariant; see companion-aria designSeeds). FLOOR 6 opens the SECOND companion's set and carries companion-design #2 (bound on join per world-logic-companion-bind; variety + safety-net laws: NOT a thread/weave/fate mechanism, NOT sexual the same way as THE LOOM; activation discoverable within floors 6-10).","enemies":[{"name":"The Unlit","role":"floor-3 room 1 — single warden, the environmental tutorial: an active plaster construct that keeps its crit-seam in shadow","readableTrait":"CRIT-SEAM-IN-SHADOW (environmental complication on the crit-read). Active combatant — initiative, strikes, durable (warded mass x0.5-0.75, open x1.0; winnable by combat) — BUT its keystone crit-seam unlocks the correct/decisive multiplier only under DIRECT LIGHT, and it orients to keep its front to the dark. In shadow a targeted 'crit' strike lands on unlit mass (a tactical whiff, not a mirror-punish). CORRECT (x1.5-2.0): bring light onto it FIRST — carry the Cold Lantern onto its front, or drive/bait it into the room's lit patch (Aria can herd it) — exposing the crit-seam, then strike. DECISIVE (x3.0): with the seam LIT, the precise keystone strike (INT-read + FIN-placed) ends it fast. Lesson: you cannot crit what you cannot see — manage the light, THEN strike; but you CAN still grind it down in the dark, only slower and under more exposure. Construct reset on retreat (re-weave to pristine free of the rest-clock)."},{"name":"The Gutter","role":"floor-3 room 2 — single warden + FAILING-LIGHT hazard: introduces mild time-pressure","readableTrait":"FAILING LIGHT (environmental + TIME-PRESSURE). Active warden in a room whose flat lamplight GUTTERS and lets the dark spread inward turn by turn; The Gutter retreats into the growing shadow, keeping its crit-seam unlit. Fighting it blind (crit-spot dark) still works but is SLOW = more exposure as the dark takes the room. TACTIC: work the CLOCK — corner it in the last lit patch, or carry light to pin it lit, before the dark closes (Aria's 'Set the Pace' buys tempo against the spread). DECISIVE (x3.0): pinned in light, crit-seam exposed, the precise keystone strike ends it. If the room goes fully dark before the kill the crit-window is lost and a retreat re-weaves it — a real tactical setback (time-pressure is genuine), never a lethal unsolved gate. Bands as elsewhere: warded x0.5-0.75, open x1.0, lit crit-read x1.5-2.0, decisive x3.0."},{"name":"The Sconce","role":"floor-3 room 3 — staged climax warden: identify-the-true-crit-spot then strike, under shifting light (first light-touch of the multi-phase shape toward the f6-f8 curve)","readableTrait":"FALSE SEAMS (environmental + IDENTIFY layer). A larger active construct in a hall of moving light: the shifting lamplight throws REFLECTIONS and FALSE crit-glyphs across its dead-white front, so several 'crit-seams' show at once and only ONE is the true keystone (the line where the plaster actually last closed; the others are cast light). It fights throughout (initiative, strikes, real kill-risk) — you are NOT frozen waiting to solve; you fight while reading. Mis-targeting a false seam wastes that strike's crit (a whiff, v30 texture) and you keep fighting. CORRECT (x1.5-2.0) / DECISIVE (x3.0): read which seam is TRUE — it does not move with the light (reflections slide, the real line holds; Aria's 'Read the Table' names it; the Sunwake Flare freezes the reflections for a beat) — then the precise keystone strike on the TRUE seam ends the floor fast. Brute still chips it (x1.0 open) — winnable without the identify, only slower under sustained kill-risk. Construct reset on retreat (re-weaves; the light resets the false-seam pattern fresh)."}],"challenge":"CHALLENGE OWNER: CHARACTER (challenge-door-v3 COMBAT SPINE). SECOND ESCALATION FLOOR — a FIGHT, won by tactical play + dice. Hold the combat spine, step MAGNITUDE again (no new companion; companions arrive floors 1/6/11). Floors 1-2 made the ENEMY the thing to fight/read (static -> migrating crit-spot -> coordinated pair). Floor 3's ONE dominant NEW axis is ENVIRONMENTAL: the ROOM becomes part of the fight. These constructs (same dead-white plaster) keep their crit-seam in SHADOW — the crit multiplier unlocks only under direct light, and the light is scarce, movable, failing, or thrown into false reflections. The tactical problem is 'get light onto the crit-spot, then read+strike it' — but ORDINARY attacks still damage the warden (the fight is winnable without perfect light play, only slower and riskier), and brute stays viable-suboptimal (warded mass x0.5-0.75, open x1.0), NEVER the losing line. The crit-strike (INT-read + FIN-placed Letter-Knife) stays the optimization, now GATED behind an environmental manipulation. SIZE grows 2 rooms -> 3 rooms.\n\nTHE PAIR: Alan enters at LEVEL 3 (floors 1-2 cleared, +1 each) with the Letter-Knife + floor-2 kit (Keystone-Picks, Reader's Clasp — the Clasp's PERCEPTION/initiative directly helps the light-read), WILL LINK-bound to Aria; still fragile. Aria BOUND to LEVEL 3 beside him (world-logic-companion-bind — a peer who leveled with him; calibrate opposition for a LEVEL-3 BOUND PAIR, never unbound-Aria). 'Read the Table' names the TRUE crit-seam among false ones (room 3), 'Set the Pace' buys tempo against the failing-light clock (room 2). Real kill-risk grows: the dark hides threats, and a warden fought blind (crit-spot unlit) takes longer to bring down = more exposure — mismanaging the light is how a level-3 pair dies here, not failing a puzzle. NO UNDEALT-INFO GATE: winnable by fighting; the light-reads are tactical optimizations. Governed by world-logic-challenge-door-v3: the far door is a free threshold, the wardens are the combat gate; clearing all three rooms RISES the floor + Alan +1 (to 4; Aria's bind loosens to bound-L4). v30 elimination textures ride the light-reads (a strike in shadow lands on unlit mass; a false seam whiffs); v29 holds (Aria reads what a bound-L3 perception genuinely returns).\n\nPLAYER'S GAME = TACTICAL DECLARATIONS under fire: light the crit-spot then strike; work the failing-light clock; identify the fixed true seam before committing. The clear is WINNING THE FIGHTS. [CALIBRATION NOTE: re-founded combat-spine + bound-L3 pair per Alan's premise ruling 2026-07-13; refine to how floors 1-2 actually play.]","challengeOwner":"character"},"id":"1806ccbd-03cf-5c24-803e-b47ff3903627"}
+{"external-id":"world-logic-challenge-door","design-kind":"world-logic","subject-key":"challenge-door","content":{"kind":"world-logic","rule":"THE CHALLENGE-DOOR LAW (how a floor gates its rise — designed ahead so every floor is consistent; constraints-conditioned by the rising-floor setting policy). Each floor is ONE rising hallway with two ends: a RESIDENTIAL end (Alan's master suite + a grown room per joined companion — the hallway grows a room when a woman joins) and a CHALLENGE end that darkens to a SINGLE SHUT DOOR (canon t1/t3: 'the far shut door ... looks as if it wants something of Alan before it opens; still unentered'). THE DOOR'S PRICE IS EPISTEMIC, NEVER BRUTE: the door opens to a TRUE READING of the challenge behind it, never to force — battering is always the losing line (reading-beats-brute-force is the tower's spine, and 'wanting something of Alan' is ALWAYS a read/price the fiction can show, never a random lock or an arbitrary key-hunt). Clearing the challenge (unmaking/killing the warden[s] behind the door) makes the WHOLE FLOOR RISE — the floor itself is the elevator — and Alan levels +1 on the floor-clear (flat leveling, no XP). COMPANION CADENCE: the risen floor delivers a new woman every FIFTH height (floors 1, 6, 11, 16, ...); the four floors between are combat + household, no new woman. TWO PROGRESSIONS STAY SEPARATE: Alan climbs on combat merit alone (no floor impassable for lack of a bond); talents and THE LINK are accelerators, never keys. RETREAT-PERSISTENCE (tower-wide, per-enemy): a true-form/keystone kill is PERMANENT; a retreat from a merely-wounded enemy resets it to full on return — information persists across a retreat (the reads, the layout, the tells), HP does not.","implications":"Every floor-design in this game MUST honor this law before it lands: (a) the challenge is READABLE — it carries a weak-point/keystone the door's price rewards SEEING, and force is the losing line; a floor whose challenge can be brute-forced violates the spine and is a design defect. (b) The companion cadence fixes WHICH floors carry a companion-design (1, 6, 11, ...) vs combat+household only — the loremaker designs a new companion only for a fifth-height floor. (c) Per-floor RESET FLAVOR is set in each floor's own design within the tower-wide rule: illusion/construct floors re-weave to pristine FREE of the rest-clock (eerie, instant — e.g. floor 1's plaster Doorward); physical/organic floors reheal only on a genuine full rest, sharing the player's OWN rest-clock (a brief threshold-breather reheals neither him nor the enemy). (d) The door's 'wanting something' renders in the fiction as the price of a true read, mute-System-safe (the System never explains the read; the door simply does not open to force)."},"id":"16371d5f-82b5-50d2-ba2d-f7d6c48d1182"}
+{"external-id":"world-logic-challenge-door-v2","design-kind":"world-logic","subject-key":"challenge-door","source-ref":"PUBLISHED CANON WINS: published t13 (the far challenge-end door 'gives inward without a sound' when Alan and Aria shove it — it opens to FORCE, a threshold not a lock) + t17 (Alan reframes and Aria agrees: 'A door you shove is only a door. A door that makes you earn the far side of it is a lock' — the WARDEN, not the physical door, is the epistemic gate) + GM/Alan in-fiction canon 2026-07-13. Supersedes world-logic-challenge-door: the prior law framed the DOOR itself as opening 'to a true reading, never to force', which t13 contradicts. The designed yields to the disclosed; core substance (epistemic price, brute loses, floor rises on a true-read clear of the warden) is preserved, only the door-vs-warden framing is corrected.","supersedes":"world-logic-challenge-door","content":{"kind":"world-logic","rule":"THE CHALLENGE-GATE LAW (how a floor gates its rise — designed ahead so every floor is consistent; constraints-conditioned by the rising-floor setting policy; framing corrected to published canon t13/t17). Each floor is ONE rising hallway with two ends: a RESIDENTIAL end (Alan's master suite + a grown room per joined companion) and a CHALLENGE end that darkens to a SHUT DOOR (canon t1/t3). THE DOOR IS A THRESHOLD, NOT THE GATE: the physical challenge-end door may open FREELY — at floor 1 it 'gave inward without a sound' the moment Alan and Aria leaned on it (canon t13). Do NOT design a floor whose DOOR must be read/solved to open (a door-lock puzzle) — that contradicts floor-1 canon. THE EPISTEMIC GATE IS THE CHALLENGE ITSELF — the warden(s) the Hotel grows at the challenge end past the door; 'a door that makes you earn the far side of it is a lock' (canon t17, the Doorward IS the real lock). THE CHALLENGE'S PRICE IS EPISTEMIC, NEVER BRUTE: the warden yields only to a TRUE READING (its keystone/weak-point seen and struck precisely — INT-read, mental or FIN-placed), never to force; brute force is always the losing line (the warden mirrors force back — floor 1's x0.3). Clearing the challenge (unmaking/killing the warden[s]) is what makes the WHOLE FLOOR RISE — the floor itself is the elevator — and Alan levels +1 on the clear (flat leveling, no XP). COMPANION CADENCE: the risen floor delivers a new woman every FIFTH height (floors 1, 6, 11, 16, ...); the four floors between are combat + household, no new woman. TWO PROGRESSIONS STAY SEPARATE: Alan climbs on combat merit alone (no floor impassable for lack of a bond); talents and THE LINK are accelerators, never keys. RETREAT-PERSISTENCE (tower-wide, per-enemy): a true-form/keystone kill is PERMANENT; a retreat from a merely-wounded enemy resets it to full on return — information persists across a retreat (the reads, the layout, the tells), HP does not.","implications":"Every floor-design in this game MUST honor this law before it lands: (a) the CHALLENGE (warden) is READABLE — it carries a weak-point/keystone a true read rewards SEEING, and force is the losing line; a floor whose challenge can be brute-forced violates the spine and is a design defect. (b) The DOOR is a threshold that opens freely (canon t13) — the GATE is ALWAYS the challenge behind/at the door, NEVER a door-lock puzzle; 'the door opens when the challenge is cleared' is shorthand for 'the clear rises the floor', not 'the door itself must be solved'. (c) The companion cadence fixes WHICH floors carry a companion-design (1, 6, 11, ...) vs combat+household only. (d) Per-floor RESET FLAVOR is set in each floor's own design within the tower-wide rule: illusion/construct floors re-weave to pristine FREE of the rest-clock (eerie, instant — e.g. floor 1's plaster Doorward); physical/organic floors reheal only on a genuine full rest, sharing the player's OWN rest-clock. (e) The challenge 'wanting something of Alan' (canon t3) renders as the price of a true READ of the warden, mute-System-safe (the System never explains the read; the warden simply does not come apart to force)."},"id":"470a3449-62d0-5179-98a8-a0f676c64b51"}
+{"external-id":"world-logic-challenge-door-v3","design-kind":"world-logic","subject-key":"challenge-door","source-ref":"Alan's premise ruling 2026-07-13: 'floor one should be COMBAT, not a puzzle'; Aria scaled down to level 1 (peer); full rewind to end-of-t12, restart from the door. Supersedes challenge-door-v2 (which mandated 'epistemic, never brute — the warden yields only to a true reading, force always the losing line' — the exact puzzle-forcing rule the ruling retires).","supersedes":"world-logic-challenge-door-v2","content":{"kind":"world-logic","rule":"THE CHALLENGE-GATE LAW (v3 — COMBAT SPINE, premise-corrected per Alan's ruling that a floor's challenge is a FIGHT, not an epistemic gate). Each floor is ONE rising hallway with two ends: a RESIDENTIAL end (Alan's master suite + a grown room per joined companion) and a CHALLENGE end that darkens to a SHUT DOOR (canon t1/t3). THE DOOR IS A THRESHOLD, NOT THE GATE (unchanged from v2): the physical challenge-end door opens FREELY — at floor 1 it 'gave inward without a sound' the moment Alan and Aria leaned on it (canon t13). Never design a floor whose DOOR must be read/solved to open (a door-lock puzzle) — that contradicts floor-1 canon. THE GATE IS THE CHALLENGE ITSELF — the warden(s) the Hotel grows at the challenge end past the door. THE CHALLENGE IS COMBAT, MECHANICS-RESOLVED (v3 CORE CHANGE — supersedes v2's 'epistemic, never brute'): a floor is cleared by WINNING THE FIGHT — tactical play under pressure, dice deciding outcomes, real kill-risk. challengeOwner = CHARACTER: the player's game is his TACTICAL DECLARATIONS (what to do under pressure), not solving an information-gate. READING SURVIVES AS A TACTICAL LAYER, NOT A GATE: the tower's reading-flavor persists as a COMBAT OPTIMIZATION — a warden carries a weak-point/keystone that a TRUE READ (a PERCEPTION/INT character-challenge that yields the INFO of where it is, never the decision of what to do — v28) rewards with a damage multiplier (correct x1.5-2.0, decisive keystone x3.0), but ORDINARY attacks still do real damage (neutral x1.0) — the fight is WINNABLE without the read, only slower and riskier. BRUTE IS NO LONGER THE LOSING LINE: it is viable-but-suboptimal (a warded body may REDUCE non-keystone damage, never NULL it; the retired v2 'mirror force back, x0.3' punish is GONE). NO UNDEALT-INFO GATE anywhere: nothing about the clear may hinge on a piece of information the player was never given (v27/v28 parity holds) — a floor that can only be cleared by a single unstated insight is exactly the puzzle-defect this law now forbids. POWER-SCALE (v3, Alan-ruled): companions are BOUND to the climber's stature (world-logic-companion-bind) — a floor's opposition is calibrated for a LEVEL-MATCHED PAIR (Alan + his bound companion at the floor's level), credibly dangerous, never trivialized by an unbound ally. Clearing the challenge (killing/unmaking the warden[s]) RISES the whole floor — the floor itself is the elevator — and Alan levels +1 (flat leveling, no XP); his bound companion's bind loosens one step with him. COMPANION CADENCE unchanged: the risen floor delivers a new woman every FIFTH height (floors 1, 6, 11, 16, ...); the four between are combat + household, no new woman. TWO PROGRESSIONS STAY SEPARATE (unchanged): Alan climbs on combat merit alone (no floor impassable for lack of a bond); talents and THE LINK are accelerators, never keys. RETREAT-PERSISTENCE (tower-wide, per-enemy, unchanged): a true-form/keystone kill is PERMANENT; a retreat from a merely-wounded enemy resets it to full on return — information persists across a retreat (the reads, the layout, the tells), HP does not.","implications":"Every floor-design in this game MUST honor this law before it lands: (a) the CHALLENGE is a COMBAT encounter won by tactical play + dice, with REAL kill-risk for a level-matched pair; a floor whose clear hinges on a single unstated insight (an epistemic gate) is the puzzle-defect this law forbids. (b) READING survives ONLY as a tactical optimization — a crit-multiplier via a character-challenge read that yields info — never as the gate; the fight must be winnable at neutral damage without it. (c) The DOOR is a free threshold (canon t13); the gate is ALWAYS the challenge behind/at the door, never a door-lock puzzle; 'the door opens when the challenge is cleared' is shorthand for 'the clear rises the floor'. (d) POWER-SCALE: calibrate opposition for a BOUND level-matched pair (companion bound per world-logic-companion-bind); no floor-design may assume unbound-companion power. (e) v30 elimination textures apply to any knowledge elements kept (tactical reads); fair-play (v27/v28) + coy-oracle (v29) law bind as ever. (f) Per-floor RESET FLAVOR unchanged: illusion/construct floors re-weave to pristine FREE of the rest-clock (e.g. floor 1's plaster Doorward); physical/organic floors reheal only on a genuine full rest, sharing the player's own rest-clock. (g) COMPANION CADENCE fixes WHICH floors carry a companion-design (1, 6, 11, ...) vs combat + household only."},"id":"d26420c4-813b-52d0-99a2-08628a3e77d0"}
+{"external-id":"world-logic-companion-bind","design-kind":"world-logic","subject-key":"companion-bind","source-ref":"Alan's premise ruling 2026-07-13 (diagnosed floor-1-as-puzzle partly to Aria being OP): companions scale down to the climber's level, peers climbing together. Diegetic bind recommended by the loremaker and accepted by Alan.","content":{"kind":"world-logic","rule":"THE COMPANION BIND (how the Hotel scales a companion to her partner — Alan-ruled premise 2026-07-13, recommended by the loremaker and accepted). DIEGETIC, NOT A RETCON: a companion's HISTORY and NATURE stay fully true — Aria is and remains an ancient dragon, the weaver of fate, three thousand years deep. What is bound is her REACH — her working power while she climbs the tower beside her partner. THE MECHANISM (fits the established grows-things logic): the Hotel that grows rooms to fit its guest also FITS a companion to her partner's STATURE — a woman who climbs beside a level-N man reaches at level N. THE BIND LOOSENS AS THE PARTNER RISES: her working level tracks his, so she GROWS as he grows (one step per floor-clear, alongside his +1). LOOSEN TRAJECTORY (general rule): a bound companion's working block INTERPOLATES from her bound-arrival block toward her LATENT (pre-bind) depths, reaching latent when the partner's level equals her pre-bind level, then continuing to grow PAST latent as he climbs further (working level = his level, no ceiling). For Aria (pre-bind L3): bound-L1 (floor 1) -> bound-L2 (floor 2) -> latent-L3 fully returned (floor 3) -> past latent (floors 4+). Each floor-clear re-derives her block one step along this trajectory, PARITY with the partner's own +1 level-step, so the pair stays level-matched throughout. THE LINK IS THE THREAD (dovetail with canon t12): the LINK bond already established — 'you carry a share of his Will; it rises as his rises' — is now LITERAL and load-bearing: the same entanglement that ties her Will to his ties her whole reach to his stature, and her true depths RETURN as he climbs. THE CLIMB IS HOW SHE COMES BACK TO HERSELF: the reason to climb together is that his rise is hers — a narrative HOOK, not a nerf. SHEET RENDERING (approach — exact numbers coordinated with the GM seat, entity edits dry-run first, never applied unilaterally by the loremaker): a bound companion's sheet shows BOTH her TRUE depths (immutable, who she is — rendered latent/locked) AND her BOUND WORKING STATS (what she brings to a level-matched fight, ~the pair's current level). Her play-level pools cannot be her true-depth pools (a true MANA of ~108 renders bound at level-1-pair scale on floor 1); the working stats rise floor by floor as Alan levels. Constraint 7 (design-constraints-companion-talents — fully-statted; THE LINK couples to real growing stats) is satisfied BY the bound working stats: they ARE her real, growing stats for the duration of the climb.","implications":"(a) EVERY floor calibrates opposition for a LEVEL-MATCHED PAIR (Alan + bound companion at the floor's level) — credibly dangerous, real kill-risk, never trivialized by an unbound ally; no floor-design may assume unbound-companion power (this is the power-scale clause challenge-door-v3 references). (b) The bind applies to EVERY companion on joining, not Aria-only — each is bound to the climber's stature at her arrival floor and rises with him. (c) A companion's TALENT is BIND-INVARIANT (talents deepen, they do not level — THE LOOM fires the same at any bound working level); the bind governs WORKING STATS / reach only. (d) Entity-sheet rendering (true depths vs bound working stats) is coordinated with the GM seat and dry-run before applying — the design store declares the APPROACH; the GM owns the concrete sheet numbers. (e) Dovetails with THE LINK (canon t12): her growth literally tied to his is now the bind's mechanism, and the narrative promise (her depths return as he climbs) is a core hook to preserve in play."},"id":"981d3629-e9ea-56ed-90ff-380a27cc3419"}
+{"external-id":"world-logic-talent-activation-safety-net","design-kind":"world-logic","subject-key":"companion-talents","source-ref":"Alan ruling 2026-07-13 (talent-activation tutorial safety net)","content":{"kind":"world-logic","rule":"TALENT-ACTIVATION SAFETY NET: each companion's arc spans a five-floor set (floors 1-5 for the first girl, 6-10 for the second, 11-15 for the third, and so on from her arrival floor). If the party reaches the LAST floor of a girl's set and her talent's activation conditions remain undiscovered (talent still dormant, never fired), the System issues HER a tutorial quest — on her own pane, in the mute mechanical quest form — pointing her in the right direction. The quest gives DIRECTION, never the checklist: it composes with the hidden+experimental-activation constraint (conditions are discovered by living the relationship, never published) — the tutorial narrows the search space the way Alan's floor-1 tutorial quests did, without naming the trigger.","implications":"GM checks this at every floor transition into a set's last floor: for each companion whose set this is, if her talent has never fired, author the System tutorial quest to her pane that turn. • The quest is hers (companion-pane), not the player's — mutual System-pane canon established at t10/t12. • Composes with design-constraints-companion-talents #3: direction, never disclosure; the concrete conditions stay in the design store and the GM-side sheet only. • A talent that fires before the last floor never triggers the net (the quest exists only as the fallback)."},"id":"9b816f54-196d-53a7-b7ba-adb1b056fdaf"}
