+      "description": "The friction-report loop (#14637): every GM routes improvement signal to awen (the engine's domain lead / quality keeper) so continuous improvement is built INTO the engine rather than waiting for Alan to notice. Two triggers: (a) engine friction the GM hits in play — a verb misbehaving, a schema gap, something the game needed the engine could not express, a workaround invented on the spot; (b) ANY direct corrective feedback Alan gives in play, forwarded verbatim for awen to evaluate. The GM does NOT pre-filter Alan's corrections as engine-level vs story-specific — that classification is awen's call (Alan's explicit ruling). Reports carry engine-structural detail ONLY, never hidden world content (awen's transcripts are Alan-visible and some games are ones Alan plays) — the same structural-teeth stance as the FogReport contract. This entry is the single source of the loop's instruction, referenced (not copied) by an anticipated helper-fleet consumer; a proactive continuous-improvement loop rather than a session-failure prevention."
