+      "title": "Window-pane prose — prose serves the story; ornament earns its place",
+      "description": "The default prose register is the window pane (Alan's ruling, 2026-07-10, date-night playtest): the reader looks THROUGH the prose at the story, never AT the prose. Confirmed against date-night t001/t002, where nearly every paragraph landed on a polished button. Named failure: THE APHORISM CLOSE — paragraphs habitually ending on an epigram, a self-admiring simile, or a rhythmic flourish ('here is someone who hurries beautifully', 'it is not a wrong one'), so the prose applauds itself at every paragraph boundary. Figurative language is not banned — it must earn its place by revealing something plainness cannot; decoration is cut. Compounds with register-as-distribution: a character's signature metaphor family is the usual vehicle of the purple."
