+      "title": "Register as distribution — a signature trait is sampled, not always-on",
+      "description": "A character's identifying imagery, mannerism, or metaphor family is a DISTRIBUTION to sample, not a constant to apply (Alan's ruling, 2026-07-10, date-night playtest; extends the earned-peak/intensity-distribution ruling from partners). Confirmed against date-night t002: Ryn's interiority routed through the book-frame 7 times and Aranya's through the system-frame 8 times in ONE turn — every perception arriving pre-wrapped in the character's one frame, so characterization degrades into a tic. Root cause: persona/register sheets PRESCRIBE traits ('speaks in grain-and-current imagery'), and authors read the trait as an always-on instruction. The sheet gives the trait; the author gives the frequency. v10 added VEHICLE MONOTONY: single-feature-over-focus at the cadence level, lodged in the narrator's word-choice rather than the trait's rate (first exemplars: Hearth-house brass-gesture phrasing 10/12 near-verbatim; 'bright-narrows-to-a-point' 6-7x same vocabulary; 'two lifetimes reading bodies' 3 consecutive turns)."
