+      "description": "Invisible-turns at the structural level (Alan's ruling, 2026-07-10, date-night Glasshouse run): with sentence-level rhythm fixed (window-pane, v8), the turn cadence relocated to the BOUNDARIES — every turn opening on an ambient re-establishment slug and closing in a poised wait-state, so the fiction inhaled/exhaled in exact turn units (5/5 turns: lantern+rain status at every head; invitation/suspended-gesture/explicit-wait at every close). Each instance individually legal — in-fiction invitations are sanctioned, ambience is sanctioned — which is precisely how it evaded the per-instance gate: this failure exists only as a CROSS-TURN pattern and must be judged by counting across turns. Root mechanism: a fresh narrator seat re-orients by re-rendering the set, and a loop that hands the weave one completed beat per turn makes beat-completion and turn-boundary always coincide. v16 added the CUT-INSIDE-THE-BEAT band from the cadence probe A/B (2026-07-10): instructions alone fixed the deliberate half of cadence-tell (head/close monoculture 8/8 -> 5/8, recap scaffolding 3 -> 1) and none of the involuntary half (length CV metronomic in both games; the paragraph-grain settling-button pulse survived instruction pressure) — the calibration behind the instructions-vs-architecture rung choice, and the residual that cut-position variation cannot remove without cutting inside beats."
